{"abstract":"This Research through Design paper explores how object detection may be applied to a large digital art museum collection to facilitate new ways of encountering and experiencing art. We present the design and evaluation of an interactive application called SMKExplore, which allows users to explore a museum’s digital collection of paintings by browsing through objects detected in the images, as a novel form of open-ended exploration. We provide three contributions. First, we show how an object detection pipeline can be integrated into a design process for visual exploration. Second, we present the design and development of an app that enables exploration of an art museum’s collection. Third, we offer reflections on future possibilities for museums and HCI researchers to incorporate object detection techniques into the digitalization of museums.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Meyer, Louie Søs","Engel Aaen, Johanne","Tranberg, Anitamalina Regitse","Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Risi, Sebastian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776388"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Art","Computer vision","Experience Design","Exploratory search","Object detection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"algorithmic ways of seeing using object detection to facilitate art exploration","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776388","identifier":[{"id":"85194821101","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-36e89c8e-4de8-41b5-bd2b-cb15b82c34c9"],"keyword":["Art","Computer Vision","Experience Design","Exploratory Search","Object Detection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-999A595D22DDB832C9D963ECCFE52A4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3613904.3642157","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louie Søs","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","locid":"b55a7155-5e64-4230-b7da-94f7872e9742","name":"Meyer, Louie Søs","orcid":"0009-0008-7490-3049","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanne","key":"engelaaenpau","last":"Engel Aaen","name":"Engel Aaen, Johanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anitamalina Regitse","key":"tranbergpau","last":"Tranberg","name":"Tranberg, Anitamalina Regitse","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","locid":"f30d35c6-4320-476f-8506-481764e6009e","name":"Kun, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0778-7662","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3613904.3642157","pages":"1-18","series":"ACM Annual Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","status":"p","title":"Algorithmic Ways of Seeing: Using Object Detection to Facilitate Art Exploration"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194821101"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36e89c8e-4de8-41b5-bd2b-cb15b82c34c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Algorithmic Ways of Seeing: Using Object Detection to Facilitate Art Exploration","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776388","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Image-generation AI models have triggered a paradigm shift in how we can express ourselves in visual art. Despite their widespread use in a short amount of time, embedding these models into interactive artifacts is still largely unexplored. In this pictorial, we unpack the design and development process of GenFrame, an image generating picture frame that utilizes generative AI capabilities to mimic traditional paintings. Our work details the necessary steps to integrate generative AI into interactive artifacts and highlights important design considerations for controlling image-generation models in order to achieve specific design intents. Our insights provide interaction designers with a more comprehensive understanding and approach towards utilizing image-generation AI models for interactive artifacts. A demo can be viewed at https://youtu.be/1rhW4fazaBY.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809172"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cultural heritage","Interaction design","Museums"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genframe embedding generative ai into interactive artifacts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809172","identifier":[{"id":"85198907112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"keyword":["cultural heritage","image-generation AI models","interaction design","museums"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6705AE38DF230903B57FF9F32135C96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444850486/GenFrame_Embedding_Generative_AI_Into_Interactive_Artifacts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias Anton","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","name_org":"Freiberger, Matthias Anton","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3660750","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"714-727","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198907112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GenFrame – Embedding Generative AI Into Interactive Artifacts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809172","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Models leveraging both visual and textual data such as Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training (CLIP), are the backbone of many recent advances in artificial intelligence. In this work, we show that despite their versatility, such models are vulnerable to what we refer to as fooling master images. Fooling master images are capable of maximizing the confidence score of a CLIP model for a significant number of widely varying prompts, while being either unrecognizable or unrelated to the attacked prompts for humans. We demonstrate how fooling master images can be mined using stochastic gradient descent, projected gradient descent, or gradient-free optimisation. Contrary to many common adversarial attacks, the gradient-free optimisation approach allows us to mine fooling examples even when the weights of the model are not accessible. We investigate the properties of the mined fooling master images, and find that images trained on a small number of image captions potentially generalize to a much larger number of semantically related captions. Finally, we evaluate possible mitigation strategies and find that vulnerability to fooling master examples appears to be closely related to a modality gap in contrastive pre-trained multi-modal networks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Freiberger, Matthias","Kun, Peter","Igel, Christian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799221"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fooling contrastive language image pre trained models with clipmasterprints","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/445732914/Fooling_Contrastive.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799221","identifier":[{"id":"85219537520","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-32b0a564-5425-44f1-8c65-0e2a4d0f4230"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-53D3BE5C256BFF74DA1453D5EE87C02D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/445732914/Fooling_Contrastive.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=ZFZnvGXXMm","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"igelpau","last":"Igel","locid":"4ecc5e2e-7589-4f9b-9f79-d5dd99f56311","name":"Igel, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2868-0856","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["28358856"],"issue":"4","journal":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Transactions on Machine Learning Research","volume":"2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219537520"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-32b0a564-5425-44f1-8c65-0e2a4d0f4230"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fooling Contrastive Language-Image Pre-Trained Models with CLIPMasterPrints.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799221","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"With recent advances in Artificial Intelligence and increasing emphasis on human augmentation and collaboration, time is ripe for AI-enhanced support tools which empower the public to formulate and visualize a collective vision of societal issues such as climate change. Here, we report on crea.visions, a platform for human-AI co-creation within Sustainable Development Goals centered community engagement. We present in-the-wild experiments with four versions of crea.visions involving 1,000+ participants and 25,000+ generated images over three years: Versions 1 and 2 focused on developing the novel tool empowering citizens to artistically communicate their favorite abstract societal issues. In versions 3 and 4, the generic image generation GAN was replaced by custom-trained versions for Venice and Paris respectively. Refining the platform towards communityspecific action, users of version 4 can geotag their identified problems, submit solutions candidates, and are actively linked up with relevant NGOs. Finally, version 4 includes the first workflow todate which combines AI image-generating modalities of sliders and text-to-image.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rafner, Janet Frances","Zana, Blanka","Beolet, Tristan","Büyükgüzel, Safinaz","Michel, Ewen","Maiden, Neil","Risi, Sebastian","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-687345"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City St George’s, University of London"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crea visions a platform for casual co creation with a purpose envisioning the future through human ai collaboration with multiple stakeholders","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-687345","ids":["au-00dd8c5d-fc8e-4873-8a1f-1276a36476da"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AE2B6AE5988B346199469D660E2ABB58"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management, Department of Management - Center for Hybrid Intelligence"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"city st george s university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City St George’s, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Janet Frances","key":"rafnerpau","last":"Rafner","locid":"6eb09423-83bf-4190-94a5-a3f472891daa","name":"Rafner, Janet Frances","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-3334","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Blanka","key":"zanapau","last":"Zana","locid":"5624b7ca-7df2-4a0a-a505-fc1bd8e403c7","name":"Zana, Blanka","orcid":"0009-0008-6483-2742","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tristan","key":"beoletpau","last":"Beolet","name":"Beolet, Tristan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Safinaz","key":"büyükgüzelpau","last":"Büyükgüzel","locid":"f6498305-69bc-4a6f-bd6b-cfc29f8f712f","name":"Büyükgüzel, Safinaz","orcid":"0000-0002-4692-5143","rank":4,"rolecod