{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Najarro, Elias","Risi, Sebastian","Sudhakaran, Shyam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718862"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards self assembling artificial neural networks through neural developmental programs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495234/isal_a_00697.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718862","identifier":[{"id":"105007222482","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-64fc45cd-4f71-4b75-a3dd-833b32125ca2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-59704F792D60173F3B3CF5CD02225852"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108495234/isal_a_00697.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007222482"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-64fc45cd-4f71-4b75-a3dd-833b32125ca2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Self-Assembling Artificial Neural Networks through Neural Developmental Programs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718862","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"ABSTRACT Organisms in nature have evolved to exhibit flexibility in face of changes to the environment and/or to themselves. Artificial neural networks (ANNs) have proven useful for controlling of artificial agents acting in environments. However, most ANN models used for reinforcement learning-type tasks have a rigid structure that does not allow for varying input sizes. Further, they fail catastrophically if inputs are presented in an ordering unseen during optimization. We find that these two ANN inflexibilities can be mitigated and their solutions are simple and highly related. For permutation invariance, no optimized parameters can be tied to a specific index of the input elements. For size invariance, inputs must be projected onto a common space that does not grow with the number of projections. Based on these restrictions, we construct a conceptually simple model that exhibit flexibility most ANNs lack. We demonstrate the model’s properties on multiple control problems, and show that it can cope with even very rapid permutations of input indices, as well as changes in input size. Ablation studies show that is possible to achieve these properties with simple feedforward structures, but that it is much easier to optimize recurrent structures.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Winther Pedersen, Joachim","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381906"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial neural networks","Feedforward Structures","Flexibility in Artificial Agents","Permutation Invariance","Recurrent neural networks","Reinforcement learning","Size Invariance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minimal neural network models for permutation invariant agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.07868.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381906","ids":["itu-2b41decf-c75e-4ecf-be2e-497eb8f0fc66"],"keyword":["Artificial Neural Networks","Feedforward Structures","Flexibility in Artificial Agents","Permutation Invariance","Recurrent Neural Networks","Reinforcement Learning","Size Invariance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D5985B1F8364F1CBEF5BC19D5605AB79"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.07868.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"wintherpedersenpau","last":"Winther Pedersen","locid":"ff6f398b-4bde-46da-a460-9815134b42eb","name":"Winther Pedersen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-7884-9432","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2b41decf-c75e-4ecf-be2e-497eb8f0fc66"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Minimal Neural Network Models for Permutation Invariant Agents","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381906","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A successful development of a complex multicellular organism took millions of years of evolution. The genome of such a multicellular organism guides the development of its body from a single cell, including its control system. Our goal is to imitate this natural process using a single neural cellular automaton (NCA) as a genome for modular robotic agents. In the introduced approach, called Neural Cellular Robot Substrate (NCRS), a single NCA guides the growth of a robot and the cellular activity which controls the robot during deployment. We also introduce three benchmark environments, which test the ability of the approach to grow different robot morphologies. We evolve the NCRS with covariance matrix adaptation evolution strategy (CMA-ES), and covariance matrix adaptation MAP-Elites (CMA-ME) for quality diversity and observe that CMA-ME generates more diverse robot morphologies with higher fitness scores. While the NCRS is able to solve the easier tasks in the benchmark, the success rate reduces when the difficulty of the task increases. We discuss directions for future work that may facilitate the use of the NCRS approach for more complex domains.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pontes-Filho, Sidney","Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","Najarro, Elias","Nichele, Stefano","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383201"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","Modular Robots","Neural Cellular Automata NCA","Quality Diversity Evolution Strategies","Robot Morphogenesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a unified substrate for body brain co evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92843039/2203.12066.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383201","ids":["itu-836fa242-af47-4796-8c83-a96d8e0f0727"],"keyword":["- Evolutionary Robotics","- Modular Robots","- Neural Cellular Automata (NCA)","- Quality Diversity Evolution Strategies","- Robot Morphogenesis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F23317C3979AA9EAFAD5718CC0533DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.12066","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92843039/2203.12066.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sidney","key":"pontesfilhopau","last":"Pontes-Filho","name":"Pontes-Filho, Sidney","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathryn Elizabeth","key":"walkerpau","last":"Walker","name":"Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefano","key":"nichelepau","last":"Nichele","name":"Nichele, Stefano","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-836fa242-af47-4796-8c83-a96d8e0f0727"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Unified Substrate for Body-Brain Co-evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383201","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Deep generative models can automatically create content of diverse types. However, there are no guarantees that such content will satisfy the criteria necessary to present it to end-users and be functional, e.g. the generated levels could be unsolvable or incoherent. In this paper we study this problem from a geometric perspective, and provide a method for reliable interpolation and random walks in the latent spaces of Categorical VAEs based on Riemannian geometry. We test our method with “Super Mario Bros” and “The Legend of Zelda” levels, and against simpler baselines inspired by current practice. Results show that the geometry we propose is better able to interpolate and sample, reliably staying closer to parts of the latent space that decode to playable content.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gonzalez-Duque, Miguel","Palm, Rasmus Berg","Hauberg, Søren","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S02-080.49-036159"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","end":"2022-08-24","place":"Beijing , cn","start":"2022-08-21","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Categorical VAEs","Content validity","Deep generative models","Differential geometry","Procedural Content Generation","Riemannian geometry","Uncertainty quantification","Variational autoencoders"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mario plays on a manifold generating functional content in latent space through differential geometry","src":["dtu","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277788909/2206.00106.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-080.49-036159","identifier":[{"id":"85139163312","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9d00f8d2-24e6-4f70-bf8f-8854a1694405","itu-58a42470-21e0-4566-a7f4-b5ed073329c8"],"keyword":["Categorical VAEs","Content Validity","Deep Generative Models","Differential Geometry","Procedural Content Generation","Riemannian Geometry","Uncertainty Quantification","Variational Autoencoders"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B27AE10AE23C8ADD0FC4E2D6007FC14D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.00106","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277788909/2206.00106.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Gonzalez","key":"duquepau","last":"Duque","name":"Duque, Miguel Gonzalez","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Berg","key":"palmpau","last":"Palm","name":"Palm, Rasmus Berg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"haubergpau","last":"Hauberg","locid":"fcd72947-62e1-4706-92bb-8451a1935d8d","name":"Hauberg, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-7223-877X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cog51982.2022.9893612","isbn":["9781665459907"],"issn":["23254289"],"journal":"Proceedings of the 2022 IEEE Conference on Games","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 IEEE Conference on Games","title_org":"Proceedings of the 2022 IEEE Conference on Games (CoG)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139163312"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9d00f8d2-24e6-4f70-bf8f-8854a1694405","itu-58a42470-21e0-4566-a7f4-b5ed073329c8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mario Plays on a Manifold: Generating Functional Content in Latent Space through Differential Geometry","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.49-036159","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In contrast to deep reinforcement learning agents, biological neural networks are grown through a self-organized developmental process. Here we propose a new hypernetwork approach to grow artificial neural networks based on neural cellular automata (NCA). Inspired by self-organising systems and information-theoretic approaches to developmental biology, we show that our HyperNCA method can grow neural networks capable of solving common reinforcement learning tasks. Finally, we explore how the same approach can be used to build developmental metamorphosis networks capable of transforming their weights to solve variations of the initial RL task.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Najarro, Elias","Sudhakaran, Shyam","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381397"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biological neural networks","HyperNCA","Neural Cellular Automata","metamorphosis networks","self organized developmental process"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypernca growing developmental networks with neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11674","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381397","ids":["itu-099e48ae-434e-48d0-ad58-ec423e84d5d1"],"keyword":["HyperNCA","biological neural networks","metamorphosis networks","neural cellular automata","self-organized developmental process"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CD59130E627483E1D80EA92262A79812"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92842983/10.4324_9780429355950_14_chapterpdf.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11674","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19765541"],"issn_org":["23318422"],"journal":"arXiv","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p","title":"arXiv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-099e48ae-434e-48d0-ad58-ec423e84d5d1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HyperNCA: Growing Developmental Networks with Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381397","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In nature, the process of cellular growth and differentiation has lead to an amazing diversity of organisms --- algae, starfish, giant sequoia, tardigrades, and orcas are all created by the same generative process. Inspired by the incredible diversity of this biological generative process, we propose a generative model, the Variational Neural Cellular Automata (VNCA), which is loosely inspired by the biological processes of cellular growth and differentiation. Unlike previous related works, the VNCA is a proper probabilistic generative model, and we evaluate it according to best practices. We find that the VNCA learns to reconstruct samples well and that despite its relatively few parameters and simple local-only communication, the VNCA can learn to generate a large variety of output from information encoded in a common vector format. While there is a significant gap to the current state-of-the-art in terms of generative modeling performance, we show that the VNCA can learn a purely self-organizing generative process of data. Additionally, the self-organizing nature bestows the VNCA with some inherent robustness against perturbations in the early stages of growth.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Berg Palm, Rasmus","Duque, Miguel Gonzalez","Sudhakaran, Shyam","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383329"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cellular growth","Differentiation","Probabilistic generative model","Self organizing systems","Variational Neural Cellular Automata"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variational neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=7fFO4cMBx_9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383329","identifier":[{"id":"85150339151","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8caad5b5-0bd5-4f8e-9642-c083a9d8ffed"],"keyword":["Cellular growth","Differentiation","Probabilistic generative model","Self-organizing systems","Variational Neural Cellular Automata"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1579E9A41AADE4F83A48D61809B6D6B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=7fFO4cMBx_9","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Gonzalez","key":"duquepau","last":"Duque","name":"Duque, Miguel Gonzalez","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"International Conference on Learning Representations","status":"p","title":"International Conference on Learning Representations","title_org":"International Conference on Learning Representations 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8caad5b5-0bd5-4f8e-9642-c083a9d8ffed"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Variational Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383329","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Grabe, Imke","Duque, Miguel Gonzalez","Risi, Sebastian","Zhu, Jichen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383855"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a framework for human ai interaction patterns in co creative gan applications","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3124/paper9.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383855","ids":["itu-b14bfa2e-0264-4e42-b1de-f003f53a913b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9839D2B3468525DEC23E3D639F7B7B61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3124/paper9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Imke","key":"grabepau","last":"Grabe","locid":"7c852728-c562-4df0-84c1-4488dde7c360","name":"Grabe, Imke","orcid":"0000-0002-5122-6769","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miguel Gonzalez","key":"duquepau","last":"Duque","name":"Duque, Miguel Gonzalez","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Joint Proceedings of the ACM IUI Workshops 2022, March 2022, Helsinki, Finland"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b14bfa2e-0264-4e42-b1de-f003f53a913b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards a Framework for Human-AI Interaction Patterns in Co-Creative GAN Applications","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383855","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Materials with the ability to self-classify their own shape have the potential to advance a wide range of engineering applications and industries. Biological systems possess the ability not only to self-reconfigure but also to self-classify themselves to determine a general shape and function. Previous work into modular robotics systems has only enabled self-recognition and self-reconfiguration into a specific target shape, missing the inherent robustness present in nature to self-classify. In this paper we therefore take advantage of recent advances in deep learning and neural cellular automata, and present a simple modular 2D robotic system that can infer its own class of shape through the local communication of its components. Furthermore, we show that our system can be successfully transferred to hardware which thus opens opportunities for future self-classifying machines. Code available at https://github.com/kattwalker/projectcube. Video available at https://youtu.be/0TCOkE4keyc.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","Berg Palm, Rasmus","Moreno, Rodrigo","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381412"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomimetics","Deep learning","Modular robotics","Neural Cellular Automata","self classifying systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"physical neural cellular automata for 000000000002d shape classification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90884499/project_cube_for_IROS_2022_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381412","ids":["itu-0a957b67-d70e-453c-8f8b-bd5c0e3311e6"],"keyword":["biomimetics","deep learning","modular robotics","neural cellular automata","self-classifying systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-078E5851A4A04C7A48C21E04D5594FE1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90884499/project_cube_for_IROS_2022_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathryn Elizabeth","key":"walkerpau","last":"Walker","name":"Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rodrigo Moreno","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","locid":"5c54c44a-9eaa-4a97-a78a-e853dc73e9d9","name":"Moreno, Rodrigo","name_org":"Garcia, Rodrigo Moreno","orcid":"0000-0003-3738-010X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"IROS","status":"p","title":"IROS","title_org":"IROS 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0a957b67-d70e-453c-8f8b-bd5c0e3311e6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Physical Neural Cellular Automata for 2D Shape Classification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381412","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Recent work has shown promising results using Hebbian meta-learning to solve hard reinforcement learning problems and adapt-to a limited degree-to changes in the environment. In previous works each synapse has its own learning rule. This allows each synapse to learn very specific learning rules and we hypothesize this limits the ability to discover generally useful Hebbian learning rules. We hypothesize that limiting the number of Hebbian learning rules through a \"genomic bottleneck\" can act as a regularizer leading to better generalization across changes to the environment. We test this hypothesis by decoupling the number of Hebbian learning rules from the number of synapses and systematically varying the number of Hebbian learning rules. We thoroughly explore how well these Hebbian meta-learning networks adapt to changes in their environment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Palm, Rasmus Berg","Najarro, Elias","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383522"],"event":{"acronym":"NeurIPS","title":"Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Genomic Bottleneck","Hebbian learning","Meta learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testing the genomic bottleneck hypothesis in hebbian meta learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2011.06811","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383522","identifier":[{"id":"85131026589","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9a449cd6-cfcc-420c-bd71-91b46953b610"],"keyword":["Genomic Bottleneck","Hebbian learning","Meta learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-4D89DCA0B6722F767CFEC70959E461CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2011.06811","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.06811","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Berg","key":"palmpau","last":"Palm","name":"Palm, Rasmus Berg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2011.06811","issn":["26403498"],"journal":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Machine Learning Research","volume":"148"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131026589"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9a449cd6-cfcc-420c-bd71-91b46953b610"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Testing the Genomic Bottleneck Hypothesis in Hebbian Meta-Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383522","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Vi introducerer en ny combination af Baysianske modeller (BM) og neurale netværk (NN) med det formål at lave prediktioner med et minimum af forventet risiko. Vores tilgang kombinerer det bedste af begge verdener, dataeffektiviteten og fortolkbarheden af en BM og et NNs hastighed. For at lave forudsigelser med en BM med den lavest mulige forventede fejl kræver integration over posterior fordelingen. Når eksakt følgeslutning af posterior prediktationsfordelingen er umedgørlig benyttes ofte approksimationsmetoder såsom Monte Carlo (MC) simulering. Med MC aftager variansen af estimatoren med antallet af eksempler, men på bekostning af øget beregningsomkostning. Vores tilgang fjerner behovet for den iterative MC simulering på CPUen til forudsigelser. Vores tilgang fungerer ved at træne et NN med syntetisk data genereret ved hjælp af den BM. Med en enkel, fremadrettet passage af data giver det NN en punktmæssig approksimation til den BMs posterior prediktive fordeling for en given observation. Vi opnår således risiko minimerede forudsigelser signifikant hurtigere end MC simulering med et ubetydeligt tab i præcision i test datasættet. Vi kombinerer denne metode med aktiv læring for a minimere mængden af data krævet for at træne det NN. Dette er gjort ved iterativt at etikere mere data i regioner forbundet med høj usikkerhed hos det NN.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Löwe, Mathias","Lunnemann, Per","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384024"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Bayesian models","Expected risk minimization","Monte Carlo simulation","Neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid risk minimization with bayesian models through deep learning approximation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384024","ids":["itu-bcb21c72-b66f-477d-9ce3-977454af9286"],"keyword":["Active learning","Bayesian models","Expected risk minimization","Monte Carlo simulation","Neural networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-01A6110F48DB0FCB5635D9CE5A9C9CBC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Blackwood Seven Danmark A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"löwepau","last":"Löwe","name":"Löwe, Mathias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"lunnemannpau","last":"Lunnemann","name":"Lunnemann, Per","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","blackwood seven danmark a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bcb21c72-b66f-477d-9ce3-977454af9286"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rapid Risk Minimization with Bayesian Models Through Deep Learning Approximation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384024","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces EvoCraft, a framework for Minecraft designed to study open-ended algorithms. We introduce an API that provides an open-source Python interface for communicating with Minecraft to place and track blocks. In contrast to previous work in Minecraft that focused on learning to play the game, the grand challenge we pose here is to automatically search for increasingly complex artifacts in an open-ended fashion. Compared to other environments used to study open-endedness, Minecraft allows the construction of almost any kind of structure, including actuated machines with circuits and mechanical components. We present initial baseline results in evolving simple Minecraft creations through both interactive and automated evolution. While evolution succeeds when tasked to grow a structure towards a specific target, it is unable to find a solution when rewarded for creating a simple machine that moves. Thus, EvoCraft offers a challenging new environment for automated search methods (such as evolution) to find complex artifacts that we hope will spur the development of more open-ended algorithms. A Python implementation of the EvoCraft framework is available at: github.com/real-itu/Evocraft-py.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Berg Palm, Rasmus","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382906"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evocraft a new challenge for open endedness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382906","ids":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"keyword":["Evolutionary computation","MIECRAFT","OPEN ENDED EVOLUTION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3563055C60A4A0D2D68E0538909CC59"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421848/2012.04751.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"bergpalmpau","last":"Berg Palm","name":"Berg Palm, Rasmus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","status":"p","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6e406c79-2b12-4d2d-a7ab-a2aa0aedef80"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EvoCraft: A New Challenge for Open-Endedness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382906","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Neural Cellular Automata (NCAs) have been proven effective in simulating morphogenetic processes, the continuous construction of complex structures from very few starting cells. Recent developments in NCAs lie in the 2D domain, namely reconstructing target images from a single pixel or infinitely growing 2D textures. In this work, we propose an extension of NCAs to 3D, utilizing 3D convolutions in the proposed neural network architecture. Minecraft is selected as the environment for our automaton since it allows the generation of both static structures and moving machines. We show that despite their simplicity, NCAs are capable of growing complex entities such as castles, apartment blocks, and trees, some of which are composed of over 3,000 blocks. Additionally, when trained for regeneration, the system is able to regrow parts of simple functional machines, significantly expanding the capabilities of simulated morphogenetic systems. The code for the experiment in this paper can be found at: https://github.com/real-itu/3d-artefacts-nca.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sudhakaran, Shyam","Grbic, Djordje","Li, Siyan","Katona, Adam","Najarro, Elias","Glanois, Claire","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383561"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cellular automata","Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","Open ended evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growing 000000000003d artefacts and functional machines with neural cellular automata","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383561","identifier":[{"id":"86000272077","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"keyword":["Minecraft","Neural Cellular Automata","cellular automata","open ended evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F452FA7C08B2A4307CD75B7EBE9D26C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86421939/isal_a_00451.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shyam","key":"sudhakaranpau","last":"Sudhakaran","locid":"b4a6e67f-0caa-4faf-a136-bf77496f3659","name":"Sudhakaran, Shyam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Siyan","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"71efb6df-0032-4f63-9a05-8489aedd9023","name":"Li, Siyan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"katonapau","last":"Katona","name":"Katona, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elias","key":"najarropau","last":"Najarro","locid":"98a59a44-499e-4a6e-a8e8-24211f117b23","name":"Najarro, Elias","orcid":"0000-0002-7875-3251","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"glanoispau","last":"Glanois","locid":"f2b81a70-1d6c-42d1-a3b5-1d4338be4b8c","name":"Glanois, Claire","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","volume":"2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000272077"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9cfbe7f0-0225-46d0-ac0e-eaca10caa909"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Growing 3D Artefacts and Functional Machines with Neural Cellular Automata","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383561","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Robots are still missing the ability to adapt to new environments. However, biological systems are able to adapt to new environments with ease; perhaps because they have the ability to react to en- vironmental input during a growth phase with changes not only in behaviour, but also morphology. Yet within the field of robots, environmental based development of morphology is an under re- searched area. In this paper we use an evolutionary algorithm to evolve neural cellular automata capable of inducing environmental based developmental plasticity in robots. We use the kinetic energy of each cell and its neighbours as an input to our network, the out- put of which determines the position of new cell growth. We evolve our neural cellular automata first in three individual environments and then also for performance in multiple environments. We show that the networks that use environmental feedback outperform those that do not and that by introducing environmental feedback during development, more adaptive and better performing robots are potentially possible.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381330"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Helmut Hauser"],"keyword":["Adaptive Robotics","Environmental Plasticity","Evolutionary algorithms","Morphological Development","Neural Cellular Automata"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"growing simulated robots with environmental feedback an eco evo devo approach","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3449726.3459514","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381330","identifier":[{"id":"85111025440","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-04c939eb-355f-41c3-b418-88aff5a9251c"],"keyword":["Adaptive Robotics","Environmental Plasticity","Evolutionary Algorithms","Morphological Development","Neural Cellular Automata"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-604B6CDB8A1DFBC32A5CA8A25D897DED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3449726.3459514","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86418533/gecco_reduced_version_v2.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"helmut hauser","name":"Helmut Hauser","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathryn Elizabeth","key":"walkerpau","last":"Walker","name":"Walker, Kathryn Elizabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3449726.3459514","journal":"GECCO","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GECCO"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111025440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-04c939eb-355f-41c3-b418-88aff5a9251c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Growing Simulated Robots with Environmental Feedback: an Eco-Evo-Devo Approach","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381330","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Random exploration is one of the main mechanisms through which reinforcement learning (RL) finds well-performing policies. However, it can lead to undesirable or catastrophic outcomes when learning online in safety-critical environments. In fact, safe learning is one of the major obstacles towards real-world agents that can learn during deployment. One way of ensuring that agents respect hard limitations is to explicitly configure boundaries in which they can operate. While this might work in some cases, we do not always have clear a-priori information which states and actions can lead dangerously close to hazardous states. Here, we present an approach where an additional policy can override the main policy and offer a safer alternative action. In our instinct-regulated RL (IR2L) approach, an “instinctual” network is trained to recognize undesirable situations, while guarding the learning policy against entering them. The instinct network is pre-trained on a single task where it is safe to make mistakes, and transferred to environments in which learning a new task safely is critical. We demonstrate IR2L in the OpenAI Safety gym domain, in which it receives a significantly lower number of safety violations during training than a baseline RL approach while reaching similar task performance.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381718"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Life long learning","Reinforcement learning","Safe reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safer reinforcement learning through transferable instinct networks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422010/isal_a_00449.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381718","identifier":[{"id":"86000265479","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e472bea-7f01-4e7a-a4ab-b9ac2c193e86"],"keyword":["Life-long learning","Reinforcement learning","safe reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F89D1E98E7D256336E700FC19E45C698"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86422010/isal_a_00449.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["26931508"],"issue":"2021","journal":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000265479"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e472bea-7f01-4e7a-a4ab-b9ac2c193e86"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safer Reinforcement Learning through Transferable Instinct Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this technical demonstration paper we document the use of a Generative Adversarial Network (GAN) based casual creator game for systematic assessment of human creativity. We discuss some of the challenges in designing GAN-based casual creators, specifically focusing on how to identify and select appropriate parts of the latent vector space - images, in our case.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Gajdacz, Miroslav","Rafner, Janet Frances","Langsford, Steven William","Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","Bergenholtz, Carsten","Biskjaer, Michael Mose","Noy, Lior","Risi, Sebastian","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-135201"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-18","place":"Virtual, Online, mx","start":"2021-09-14","title":"12th International Conference on Computational Creativity, ICCC 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crea blender a gan based casual creator for creativity assessment","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://computationalcreativity.net/iccc21/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-135201","identifier":[{"id":"85156213647","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0a59885d-fb4d-427d-9beb-3dc5e8885f42"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A0362B9BCD72F68C51CDD97098988B0C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"]