{"abstract":"The advent of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) bring human-AI interaction to the forefront of HCI research. This paper argues that games are an ideal domain for studying and experimenting with how humans interact with AI. Through a systematic survey of neural network games (n = 38), we identified the dominant interaction metaphors and AI interaction patterns in these games. In addition, we applied existing human-AI interaction guidelines to further shed light on player-AI interaction in the context of AI-infused systems. Our core finding is that AI as play can expand current notions of human-AI interaction, which are predominantly productivity-based. In particular, our work suggests that game and UX designers should consider flow to structure the learning curve of human-AI interaction, incorporate discovery-based learning to play around with the AI and observe the consequences, and offer users an invitation to play to explore new forms of human-AI interaction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Zhu, Jichen","Villareale, Jennifer","Javvaji, Nithesh","Risi, Sebastian","Löwe, Mathias","Weigelt, Rush","Harteveld, Casper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382816"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Drexel University","Northeastern University"],"keyword":["AI infused Systems","Discovery based Learning","Human AI interaction","Neural Network Games","Player AI interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"player ai interaction what neural network games reveal about ai as play","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3411764.3445307","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382816","identifier":[{"id":"85104170761","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-66eb1199-34f5-4f8b-8c30-153651c65ce9"],"keyword":["AI-infused Systems","Discovery-based Learning","Human-AI Interaction","Neural Network Games","Player-AI Interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-33BD6D65CE757F25AD2EC979B950CEAA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3411764.3445307","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86438685/2101.06220v1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3411764.3445307","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Procedural eXpression Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"drexel university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Drexel University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"northeastern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northeastern University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","locid":"e383647f-00d3-41b1-ad95-ff69bdfffb42","name":"Zhu, Jichen","orcid":"0000-0001-6740-4550","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jennifer","key":"villarealepau","last":"Villareale","name":"Villareale, Jennifer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nithesh","key":"javvajipau","last":"Javvaji","name":"Javvaji, Nithesh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias","key":"löwepau","last":"Löwe","name":"Löwe, Mathias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rush","key":"weigeltpau","last":"Weigelt","name":"Weigelt, Rush","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"harteveldpau","last":"Harteveld","name":"Harteveld, Casper","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3411764.3445307","eisbn":["9781450380966"],"status":"p","title":"CHI '21: Proceedings of the 2021 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-66eb1199-34f5-4f8b-8c30-153651c65ce9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Player-AI Interaction: What Neural Network Games Reveal About AI as Play","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382816","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a Mixed-Initiative version of Squeezer, a tool for designing juice effects in the Unity game engine. Drawing upon sound synthesizers and game description languages, Squeezer can synthesize common types of juice effects by combining simple building blocks into sequences. Additionally, Squeezer offers effect generation based on predefined recipes as well as an interface for interactively evolving effect sequences. We conducted a user study with five experts to verify the functionality and interest among game designers. By applying generative and evolutionary strategies to juice effect design, Squeezer allows game designers and researchers using games in their work to explore adding juice effects to their games and frameworks. Squeezer is available at: https://github.com/pyjamads/Squeezer","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Mads","Pichlmair, Martin","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383423"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","end":"2021-08-06","place":"Fully Online","start":"2021-08-02","title":"FDG 2021: Foundations of Digital Games","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Generative design strategies","Juice Effects","Mixed initiative tools","Sound synthesis","Unity game engine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"squeezer a mixed initiative tool for designing juice effects","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3472538.3472575","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383423","identifier":[{"id":"85118238023","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-92eafb4f-70ba-42f8-a317-90746d2b4d4f"],"keyword":["Generative design strategies","Juice effects","Mixed-initiative tools","Sound synthesis","Unity game engine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7844109C88C62C31017234C9A0B1FA25"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3472538.3472575","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86237995/Squeezer_Evolution_FDG_pure.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Creative AI Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"pichlmairpau","last":"Pichlmair","locid":"ddcdfda8-c5ea-4e67-b0ea-21ba86966197","name":"Pichlmair, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-8828-9723","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3472538.3472575","eisbn":["9781450384223/21/08"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 16th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games (FDG) 2021 (FDG’21)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118238023"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-92eafb4f-70ba-42f8-a317-90746d2b4d4f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Squeezer - A Mixed-Initiative Tool for Designing Juice Effects","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383423","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The rise of digital technologies and Machine Learning (ML)-Tools for creative expression brings about novel opportunities for studying creativity and cognition at scale. In this paper, we present a pilot study of crea.blender SDG-an online GAN based image generation game. We designed crea.blender SDG with two goals in mind: The first, to let people create images relating to the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and through them, engage in large-scale conversations on complex socioscientific problems. The second, as a fun and inspiring gateway for public participation in research, generating data for the creativity and cognition research and design community. Specifically in this pilot, we study and affirm that the design of crea.blender SDG is flexible enough to allow users to create images that express both anxiety and hope for the future; affirm that user generated images express these ideas in ways that are meaningful to people other than the original creator; and begin to investigate which specific features of images are more closely related to dystopian or utopian ideas of the future. Finally, we discuss implications for future design and research with ML-based creativity tools.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rafner, Janet Frances","Langsford, Steven William","Philipsen, Lotte","Risi, Sebastian","Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","Simon, Joel","Gajdacz, Miroslav","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-093.02-026785"],"event":{"acronym":"CANDC","end":"2021-06-23","place":"Virtual, Online, it","start":"2021-06-22","title":"13th Conference on Creativity and Cognition, C&amp;C '21","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Sherson, Jacob"],"keyword":["Creative Expression","Creativity and Cognition","Digital technologies","Dystopian and Utopian Imagery","GAN based Image Generation","Machine Learning Tools","Public Participation in Research","Socioscientific Problems","Sustainable development goals","User generated content"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"utopian or dystopian using a ml assisted image generation game to empower the general public to envision the future","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86612620/cc_rafner2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.02-026785","identifier":[{"id":"85109107286","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c26afeb4-d28d-4b72-8ab5-aa1e13f9ceb4","itu-1b0a6beb-78e1-4e37-9491-06e09cab6acd"],"keyword":["Creative Expression","Creativity and Cognition","Digital Technologies","Dystopian and Utopian Imagery","GAN-based Image Generation","Machine Learning Tools","Public Participation in Research","Socioscientific Problems","Sustainable Development Goals","User-Generated Content"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A59E5B9ECD59BE43FAB1778E2A244696"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86612620/cc_rafner2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janet","key":"rafnerpau","last":"Rafner","locid":"6eb09423-83bf-4190-94a5-a3f472891daa","name":"Rafner, Janet Frances","name_org":"Rafner, Janet","orcid":"0000-0001-9264-3334","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven","key":"langsfordpau","last":"Langsford","locid":"e0ee626b-3819-4a48-846c-1ff55e29aa7e","name":"Langsford, Steven William","name_org":"Langsford, Steven","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte","key":"philipsenpau","last":"Philipsen","locid":"abaa2f78-751f-4b9f-a35d-32379f9212c9","name":"Philipsen, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0002-5372-4374","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arthur","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"b6da5c3f-dc2f-4376-a964-cec167d512e6","name":"Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","name_org":"Hjorth, Arthur","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joel","key":"simonpau","last":"Simon","name":"Simon, Joel","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Miroslav","key":"gajdaczpau","last":"Gajdacz","locid":"e1804946-13cc-479c-b1e8-9b216f8c2cf5","name":"Gajdacz, Miroslav","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"shersonpau","last":"Sherson","locid":"3d8e1590-c4fa-495b-81b4-588fe374b36c","name":"Sherson, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0001-6048-587X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3450741.3466815","isbn":["9781450383769"],"place":"United States","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series","status":"p","title":"Creativity and cognition (C&amp;C '21)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109107286"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c26afeb4-d28d-4b72-8ab5-aa1e13f9ceb4","itu-1b0a6beb-78e1-4e37-9491-06e09cab6acd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Utopian or Dystopian? : Using a ML-Assisted image generation game to empower the general public to envision the future","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.02-026785","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"An important goal in reinforcement learning is to create agents that can quickly adapt to new goals but at the same time avoid situations that might cause damage to themselves or their environments. One way agents learn is through exploration mechanisms, which are needed to discover new policies. However, in deep reinforcement learning, exploration is normally done by injecting noise in the action space. While performing well in many domains, this setup has the inherent risk that the noisy actions lead agents to unsafe environment states. In this paper, we introduce a novel approach called Meta-Learned Instinctual Networks (MLIN) that allows agents to perform lifetime learning while avoiding hazardous states. At the core of the approach is a plastic network trained through reinforcement learning and an evolved \"instinctual\" network, which does not change during the agent's lifetime but can modulate the noisy output of the plastic network. We test our idea on a simple 2D navigation task with hazard zones, in which the agent has to learn to approach new targets during deployment. While a standard meta-trained network performs poorly in these tasks, MLIN allows agents to learn to navigate to new targets while minimizing collisions with hazard zones. These results suggest that meta-learning augmented with an instinctual network is a promising approach for safe AI.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382937"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life long learning","Reinforcement learning","Safe reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safer reinforcement learning through evolved instincts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571059/GECCO_2020_Grbic_Risi_POSTER.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382937","identifier":[{"id":"85089735740","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-704b619d-f68e-4cf8-824d-39507d649551"],"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","Life-long learning","Reinforcement learning","safe reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10A42B9ABCF563F3F4F9E053D00AA3F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85571059/GECCO_2020_Grbic_Risi_POSTER.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3377929.3389946","isbn":["9781450371278"],"pages":"77-78","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2020 Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion","title":"GECCO '20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089735740"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-704b619d-f68e-4cf8-824d-39507d649551"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safer reinforcement learning through evolved instincts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382937","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"We present a pilot study on crea.blender, a novel co-creative game designed for large-scale, systematic assessment of distinct con- structs of human creativity. Co-creative systems are systems in which humans and computers (often with Machine Learning) col- laborate on a creative task. This human-computer collaboration raises questions about the relevance and level of human creativity and involvement in the process. We expand on, and explore aspects of these questions in this pilot study. We observe participants play through three different play modes in crea.blender, each aligned with established creativity assessment methods. In these modes, players “blend” existing images into new images under varying constraints. Our study indicates that crea.blender provides a playful experience, affords players a sense of control over the interface, and elicits different types of player behavior, supporting further study of the tool for use in a scalable, playful, creativity assessment.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rafner, Janet Frances","Hjorth, Hermes Arthur","Risi, Sebastian","Philipsen, Lotte","Dumas, Charles","Biskjaer, Michael Mose","Noy, Lior","Tylén, Kristian","Bergenholtz, Carsten","Lynch, Jesse John","Zana, Blanka","Sherson, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-097.19-027028"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI PLAY","title":"Annual Symposium on Computer-Human Interaction in Play"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rafner, Janet Frances"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Reichman University","Weizmann Institute"],"keyword":["Co creative systems","Convergent thinking","Creativity assessment","Divergent thinking","GaN","Human creativity","Pilot study","Player behavior","crea blender","human computer collaboration","image blending","machine learning in creativity","playful experience"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"crea blender a neural network based image generation game to assess creativity","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85690689/crea.blender_A_Neural_Network_Based_Image_Generation_Game.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-097.19-027028","identifier":[{"id":"85096802779","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c622b533-7285-45ed-9d0d-1567b2f820c3","itu-10613633-fd67-42cb-8564-8bb041c4f43e"],"keyword":["Co-creative systems","GAN","convergent thinking","crea.blender","creativity assessment","divergent thinking","human creativity","human-computer collaboration","image blending","machine learning in creativity","pilot study","player behavior","playful experience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8AC4E726B6C3A32203DFDCD1D88E15B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85690689/crea.blender_A_Neural_Network_Based_Image_Generation_Game.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Cop