{"abstract":"Quality Diversity algorithms (QD) evolve a set of high-performing phenotypes that each behaves as differently as possible. However, current algorithms are all elitist, which make them unable to cope with stochastic fitness functions and behavior evaluations. In fact, many of the promising applications of QD algorithms, for instance, games and robotics, are stochastic. Here we propose two new extensions to the QD-algorithm MAP-Elites — adaptive sampling and drifting-elites — and demonstrate empirically that these extensions increase the quality of solutions in a noisy artificial test function and the behavioral diversity in a 2D bipedal walker environment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Justesen, Niels","Risi, Sebastian","Mouret, Jean-Baptiste"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382857"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adaptive sampling","Behavioral Diversity","MAP Elites","Quality Diversity algorithms","Stochastic fitness functions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"map elites for noisy domains by adaptive sampling","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84783110/map_elites_noisy_justesen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382857","identifier":[{"id":"85070591106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6a50a489-18e3-4519-923f-4bb795b4478f"],"keyword":["Adaptive sampling","Behavioral diversity","MAP-Elites","Quality Diversity algorithms","Stochastic fitness functions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-877924D0CEDBBBD0FE412BBCD252FEDC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84783110/map_elites_noisy_justesen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"justesenpau","last":"Justesen","name":"Justesen, Niels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean-Baptiste","key":"mouretpau","last":"Mouret","name":"Mouret, Jean-Baptiste","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3319619.3321904","pages":"121-122","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GECCO '19","title":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070591106"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6a50a489-18e3-4519-923f-4bb795b4478f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MAP-Elites for noisy domains by adaptive sampling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382857","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Artificial life simulations are an important tool in the study of ecological phenomena that can be difficult to examine directly in natural environments. Recent work has established the soundscape as an ecologically important resource and it has been proposed that the differentiation of animal vocalizations within a soundscape is driven by the imperative of intraspecies communication. The experiments in this paper test that hypothesis in a simulated soundscape in order to verify the feasibility of intraspecies communication as a driver of acoustic niche differentiation. The impact of intraspecies communication is found to be a significant factor in the division of a soundscape’s frequency spectrum when compared to simulations where the need to identify signals from conspecifics does not drive the evolution of signalling. The method of simulating the effects of interspecies interactions on the soundscape is positioned as a tool for developing artificial life agents that can inhabit and interact with physical ecosystems and soundscapes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kadish, David","Risi, Sebastian","Beloff, Laura"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384120"],"event":{"acronym":"ECAL","title":"European Conference on Artificial Life"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acoustic Niche Differentiation","Artificial Life Simulations","Ecological Phenomena","Intraspecies Communication","Soundscape Ecology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an artificial life approach to studying niche differentiation in soundscape ecology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/isal_a_00140","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384120","ids":["itu-c3154676-7aa3-4ec7-9657-5cf5952a374a"],"keyword":["Acoustic Niche Differentiation","Artificial Life Simulations","Ecological Phenomena","Intraspecies Communication","Soundscape Ecology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B2BAD2AC6374C0902B8930F054D951D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84783073/1907.12812.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/isal_a_00140","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"kadishpau","last":"Kadish","name":"Kadish, David","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"beloffpau","last":"Beloff","name":"Beloff, Laura","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/isal_a_00140","pages":"52-59","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"The 2019 Conference on Artificial Life: A Hybrid of the European Conference on Artificial Life (ECAL) and the International Conference on the Synthesis and Simulation of Living Systems (ALIFE)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c3154676-7aa3-4ec7-9657-5cf5952a374a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An artificial life approach to studying niche differentiation in soundscape ecology","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384120","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In continual learning, an agent is exposed to a changing environment, requiring it to adapt during execution time. While traditional reinforcement learning (RL) methods have shown impressive results in various domains, there has been less progress in addressing the challenge of continual learning. Current RL approaches do not al-low the agent to adapt during execution but only during a dedicated training phase. Here we study the problem of continual learning ina 2D bipedal walker domain, in which the legs of the walker grow over its lifetime, requiring the agent to adapt. The introduced approach combines neuroevolution, to determine the starting weights of a deep neural network, and a version of deep reinforcement learning that is continually running during execution time. The proof-of-concept results show that the combined approach gives abetter generalization performance when compared to evolution or reinforcement learning alone. The hybridization of reinforcement learning and evolution opens up exciting new research directions for continually learning agents that can benefit from suitable priors determined by an evolutionary process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grbic, Djordje","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384174"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Continual Learning","Meta learning","Reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards continual reinforcement learning through evolutionary meta learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84798816/GECCO_POSTER_2019_Grbic_Risi_nocpyright.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384174","identifier":[{"id":"85070636226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c6212d40-15e2-4332-b91f-3567cc5350ca"],"keyword":["Continual learning","Meta-learning","Reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-10CA81675713F7AEDAEB03D39D22B4FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84798816/GECCO_POSTER_2019_Grbic_Risi_nocpyright.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3319619.3322044","edition":"2019","eisbn":["9781450367486"],"pages":"119-120","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Towards Continual Reinforcement Learning through Evolutionary Meta-Learning","volume":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070636226"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c6212d40-15e2-4332-b91f-3567cc5350ca"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Continual Reinforcement Learning through Evolutionary Meta-Learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384174","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces UnityVGDL, a port of the Video Game Description Language (VGDL) to the widely used Unity game engine. Our framework is based on the General Video Game AI (GVGAI) competition framework and implements its core ontology, including a forward model. It integrates the Unity Machine Learning Agents (ML-Agents) toolkit with VGDL to train and run agents in VGDL-described games. We compare baseline learning results between GVGAI and UnityVGDL across four different games and conclude that the Unity port is comparable to the GVGAI framework. UnityVGDL is available at: https://github.com/pyjamads/UnityVGDL.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Mads","Pichlmair, Martin","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383399"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Forward Model Integration","General Video Game AI GVGAI","Unity Machine Learning Agents ML Agents","UnityVGDL","Video Game Description Language VGDL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"video game description language environment for unity machine learning agents","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84660499/VGDL_in_Unity3D_Pure.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383399","identifier":[{"id":"85073116022","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-911c6c3c-967b-40f0-9669-0bc18ae75b5b"],"keyword":["Forward Model Integration","General Video Game AI (GVGAI)","Unity Machine Learning Agents (ML-Agents)","UnityVGDL","Video Game Description Language (VGDL)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5270711570AFE3CA5277F29F8B422AD7"],"oa_link":[{"a