for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1083a640-8656-4496-adcb-b609681b1c7a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolutionary computation and games tutorial","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381512","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Growing interest in eXplainable Artificial Intelligence (XAI) aims to make AI and machine learning more understandable to human users. However, most existing work focuses on new algorithms, and not on usability, practical interpretability and efficacy on real users. In this vision paper, we propose a new research area of eXplainable AI for Designers (XAID), specifically for game designers. By focusing on a specific user group, their needs and tasks, we propose a human-centered approach for facilitating game designers to co-create with AI/ML techniques through XAID. We illustrate our initial XAID framework through three use cases, which require an understanding both of the innate properties of the AI techniques and users’ needs, and we identify key open challenges","author_count":5,"contributors":["Zhu, Jichen","Liapis, Antonios","Risi, Sebastian","Bidarra, Rafael","Youngblood, G Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381641"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Drexel University","Palo Alto Research Center"],"keyword":["Co Creation with AI ML","Explainable artificial intelligence","Game Designers","Human centered design","Usability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"explainable ai for designers a human centered perspective on mixed initiative co creation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83703474/zhu_cig18.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381641","identifier":[{"id":"85054998782","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1905cb2c-0865-4aa7-898e-b11bd8f6ae3d"],"keyword":["Co-Creation with AI/ML","Game Designers","Human-Centered Design","Usability","eXplainable Artificial Intelligence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B15858D702D0CB4C5746A80F2F675322"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83703474/zhu_cig18.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"drexel university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Drexel University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"palo alto research center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Palo Alto Research Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jichen","key":"zhupau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Jichen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Antonios","key":"liapispau","last":"Liapis","name":"Liapis, Antonios","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"bidarrapau","last":"Bidarra","name":"Bidarra, Rafael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"G Michael","key":"youngbloodpau","last":"Youngblood","name":"Youngblood, G Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2018.8490433","pages":"1-8","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games (CIG)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054998782"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1905cb2c-0865-4aa7-898e-b11bd8f6ae3d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Explainable AI for designers: A human-centered perspective on mixed-initiative co-creation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381641","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Interactive Evolution (ie) has shown promise in domains where objective-driven approaches are problematic. Collaborating by branching from the evolutionary stepping stones discovered by others (cie) has allowed users to evolve a large variety of artefacts. In this paper we explore the potential of collaboratively evolving behaviours in Minecraft through an online cie system. Results suggest that it is indeed possible to solve a maze navigation task in Minecraft collaboratively, which is difficult to achieve individually. We hope that the released framework will allow others to build more complex domains, solving a series of more and more challenging tasks through many collaborating humans.","author_count":2,"contributors":["de Prado Salas, Pablo González","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383532"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative Evolutionary Innovation","Interactive Evolution","Maze Navigation","Minecraft Behaviour Evolution","Online Collaboration Systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collaborative interactive evolution in minecraft","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85051498088","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383532","identifier":[{"id":"85051498088","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9b2e2acd-d653-4324-ad54-ebefddd10ad8"],"keyword":["Collaborative Evolutionary Innovation","Interactive Evolution","Maze Navigation","Minecraft Behaviour Evolution","Online Collaboration Systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1971B462D551FC01ACB12FC50F265DAD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pablo González","key":"depradosalaspau","last":"de Prado Salas","name":"de Prado Salas, Pablo González","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3205651.3205723","eisbn":["9781450357647"],"pages":"127-128","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GECCO '18","title":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051498088"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9b2e2acd-d653-4324-ad54-ebefddd10ad8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Collaborative interactive evolution in minecraft","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383532","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"MetaCompose is a music generator based on a hybrid evolutionary technique combining FI-2POP and multi-objective optimization. In this paper we employ the MetaCompose music generator to create music in real-time that expresses different mood-states in a game-playing environment (Checkers) and present preliminary results of an experiment focusing on determining (i) if differences in player experience can be observed when using affective-dynamic music compared to static music; and (ii) if any difference is observed when the music supports the game's internal narrative/state. Participants were tasked to play two games of Checkers while listening to two (out of three) different set-ups of game-related generated music. The possible set-ups were: static expression, consistent affective expression, and random affective expression.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, Marco","Eklund, Peter","Togelius, Julian","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S02-092.90-038386"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","end":"2018-07-19","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2018-07-15","title":"2018 Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference, GECCO 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deakin University","New York University"],"keyword":["ACM proceedings","Affective Dynamic Music","Game Narrative Support","Hybrid Evolutionary Technique","Latex","Multi objective optimization","Player Experience","Text tagging"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards an experiment on perception of affective music generation using metacompose","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84082357/experiment_perception_affective.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-092.90-038386","identifier":[{"id":"85051543726","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d2a72644-936f-45cf-8ff6-5d3f06f8f259","sdu-d471d4ce-ea49-42f6-b83b-8ec5a0be8bf7"],"keyword":["ACM proceedings","Affective-Dynamic Music","Game Narrative Support","Hybrid Evolutionary Technique","LATEX","Multi-Objective Optimization","Player Experience","Text tagging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D57CE7664EFEC4B48114CC2E858F4C8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84082357/experiment_perception_affective.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Biorobotics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"deakin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Deakin University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","locid":"6e0315fe-6ee1-493f-a23d-7acc1c33cbcf","name":"Scirea, Marco","orcid":"0000-0003-4908-0526","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3205651.3205745","eisbn":["9781450357647"],"pages":"131-132","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GECCO '18 Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051543726"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d2a72644-936f-45cf-8ff6-5d3f06f8f259","sdu-d471d4ce-ea49-42f6-b83b-8ec5a0be8bf7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Towards an experiment on perception of affective music generation using MetaCompose","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.90-038386","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) are a machine learning approach capable of generating novel example outputs across a space of provided training examples. Procedural Content Generation (PCG) of levels for video games could benefit from such models, especially for games where there is a pre-existing corpus of levels to emulate. This paper trains a GAN to generate levels for Super Mario Bros using a level from the Video Game Level Corpus. The approach successfully generates a variety of levels similar to one in the original corpus, but is further improved by application of the Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy (CMA-ES). Specifically, various fitness functions are used to discover levels within the latent space of the GAN that maximize desired properties. Simple static properties are optimized, such as a given distribution of tile types. Additionally, the champion A* agent from the 2009 Mario AI competition is used to assess whether a level is playable, and how many jumping actions are required to beat it. These fitness functions allow for the discovery of levels that exist within the space of examples designed by experts, and also guide the search towards levels that fulfill one or more specified objectives.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Volz, Vanessa","Schrum, Jacob","Liu, Jialin","Lucas, Simon M","Smith, Adam","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382794"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","Southwestern University","TU Dortmund University","University of California"],"keyword":["Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy","Fitness Functions","Generative Adversarial Networks","Procedural Content Generation","Video Game Level Corpus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving mario levels in the latent space of a deep convolutional generative adversarial network","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83681354/1805.00728.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382794","identifier":[{"id":"85050613631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-65c89c47-ab0c-41d7-bbd6-0012cf208787"],"keyword":["Covariance Matrix Adaptation Evolution Strategy","Fitness Functions","Generative Adversarial Networks","Procedural Content Generation","Video Game Level Corpus"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1041F9C1A581F0A76DD221BCF32872E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83681354/1805.00728.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"tu dortmund university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Dortmund University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"southwestern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Southwestern University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vanessa","key":"volzpau","last":"Volz","name":"Volz, Vanessa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"schrumpau","last":"Schrum","name":"Schrum, Jacob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jialin","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jialin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon M","key":"lucaspau","last":"Lucas","name":"Lucas, Simon M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Adam","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3205455.3205517","eisbn":["9781450356183"],"pages":"221-228","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GECCO '18","title":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050613631"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-65c89c47-ab0c-41d7-bbd6-0012cf208787"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving Mario Levels in the Latent Space of a Deep Convolutional Generative Adversarial Network","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382794","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Bio-hybrid systems-close couplings of natural organisms with technology-are high potential and still underexplored. In existing work, robots have mostly influenced group behaviors of animals. We explore the possibilities of mixing robots with natural plants, merging useful attributes. Significant synergies arise by combining the plants' ability to efficiently produce shaped material and the robots' ability to extend sensing and decision-making behaviors. However, programming robots to control plant motion and shape requires good knowledge of complex plant behaviors. Therefore, we use machine learning to create a holistic plant model and evolve robot controllers. As a benchmark task we choose obstacle avoidance. We use computer vision to construct a model of plant stem stiffening and motion dynamics by training an LSTM network. The LSTM network acts as a forward model predicting change in the plant, driving the evolution of neural network robot controllers. The evolved controllers augment the plants' natural light-finding and tissue-stiffening behaviors to avoid obstacles and grow desired shapes. We successfully verify the robot controllers and bio-hybrid behavior in reality, with a physical setup and actual plants.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wahby, Mostafa","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Zahadat, Payam","Risi, Sebastian","Ayres, Phil","Schmickl, Thomas","Hamann, Heiko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383404"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bio hybrid systems","Machine learning","Neural network controllers","Obstacle avoidance","Plant robot interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a robot to shape your natural plant the machine learning approach to model and control bio hybrid systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83680870/1804.06682.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383404","identifier":[{"id":"85050634013","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-915ec9d9-a957-4b7a-b576-ead3874aa79c"],"keyword":["Bio-hybrid systems","Machine learning","Neural network controllers","Obstacle avoidance","Plant-robot interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88BDB2A5AE07DD362D01B8D09AE12F9E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83680870/1804.06682.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","locid":"8785f18a-1bf3-4c63-8d8b-d3e5d516ca40","name":"Zahadat, Payam","orcid":"0000-0002-4521-7428","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","name":"Ayres, Phil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmicklpau","last":"Schmickl","name":"Schmickl, Thomas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3205455.3205516","isbn":["9781450356183"],"pages":"165-172","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Conference on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation (GECCO 2018)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050634013"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-915ec9d9-a957-4b7a-b576-ead3874aa79c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Robot to Shape your Natural Plant: The Machine Learning Approach to Model and Control Bio-Hybrid Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383404","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper addresses the relationship between games and media and discusses to which extend games can be conceived as media, and how they should be studied as such. The paper proposes a revised version of Elleström’s intermedial framework that has been harnessed to better describe games. The framework acknowledges the heterogeneous nature of not only games but all media. Elleström’s framework allows us to address games as particular tangible objects in the world in a way that avoids normative assumptions about games in general as well as specific types of games such as digital or analog games. This framework has several usages. It can be applied in an analysis the relationship between different modalities in a single game; it can be used to compare different games; and finally, it can be used to discuss the similarities and differences between games and other media objects.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383531"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","title":"Foundations of Digital Games"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Comparison","Games","Intermediality","MODES","Media","Mediation","Modalities","cybertext"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"media and games an intermedial framework","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83586834/Media_and_games_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383531","identifier":[{"id":"85055499614","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9b05e2a2-e7e5-4052-ae35-46917ea20ece"],"keyword":["Intermediality","Mediation","comparison","cybertext","games","media","modalities","modes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B3D15D13F89BB17FFD8D35CAD4C947B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83586834/Media_and_games_post_print.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steve","key":"dahlskogpedh","last":"Dahlskog","name":"Dahlskog, Steve","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian","key":"deterdingpedh","last":"Deterding","name":"Deterding, Sebastian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"fontpedh","last":"Font","name":"Font, José","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mitu","key":"khandakerpedh","last":"Khandaker","name":"Khandaker, Mitu","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carl Magnus","key":"olssonpedh","last":"Olsson","name":"Olsson, Carl Magnus","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipedh","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoph","key":"salgepedh","last":"Salge","name":"Salge, Christoph","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3235765.3235794","eisbn":["978 14503 6571 0"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Foundations of Digital Games Conference Proceedings","status":"p","subtitle":"August 7–10, 2018, Malmö, Sweden","title":"FDG '18 Proceedings of the 13th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055499614"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9b05e2a2-e7e5-4052-ae35-46917ea20ece"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Media and games: an intermedial framework","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383531","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes an approach that combines generative adversarial networks (GANs) with interactive evolutionary computation (IEC). While GANs can be trained to produce lifelike images, they are normally sampled randomly from the learned distribution, providing limited control over the resulting output. On the other hand, interactive evolution has shown promise in creating various artifacts such as images, music and 3D objects, but traditionally relies on a hand-designed evolvable representation of the target domain. The main insight in this paper is that a GAN trained on a specific target domain can act as a compact and robust genotype-to-phenotype mapping (i.e. most produced phenotypes do resemble valid domain artifacts). Once such a GAN is trained, the latent vector given as input to the GAN's generator network can be put under evolutionary control, allowing controllable and high-quality image generation. In this paper, we demonstrate the advantage of this novel approach through a user study in which participants were able to evolve images that strongly resemble specific target images.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bontrager, Philip","Lin, Wending","Togelius, Julian","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384771"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","OECD"],"country":["China","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications","New York University"],"keyword":["Generative Adversarial Networks GANs","Genotype Phenotype Mapping","Image Generation","Interactive Evolutionary Computation IEC","Latent Space Evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep interactive evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83701144/bontrager_evomusart18.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384771","identifier":[{"id":"85044656652","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-edd7552f-1aee-4a63-86d8-480b838d0097"],"keyword":["Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs)","Genotype-Phenotype Mapping","Image Generation","Interactive Evolutionary Computation (IEC)","Latent Space Evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7774F001AFC1ED2D3D2F055B5C548002"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83701144/bontrager_evomusart18.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"beijing university of posts and telecommunications","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"bontragerpau","last":"Bontrager","name":"Bontrager, Philip","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Wending","key":"linpau","last":"Lin","name":"Lin, Wending","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-77583-8_18","eisbn":["9783319775838"],"isbn":["9783319775821"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"267-282","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"EvoMUSART 2018","title":"International Conference on Computational Intelligence in Music, Sound, Art and Design"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044656652"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-edd7552f-1aee-4a63-86d8-480b838d0097"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep interactive evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384771","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"MetaCompose is a music generator based on a hybrid evolutionary technique that combines FI-2POP and multi-objective optimization. In this paper we employ the MetaCompose music generator to create music in real-time that expresses different mood-states in a game-playing environment (Checkers). In particular, this paper focuses on determining if differences in player experience can be observed when: (i) using affective-dynamic music compared to static music, and (ii) the music supports the game's internal narrative/state. Participants were tasked to play two games of Checkers while listening to two (out of three) different set-ups of game-related generated music. The possible set-ups were: static expression, consistent affective expression, and random affective expression. During game-play players wore a E4 Wristband, allowing various physiological measures to be recorded such as blood volume pulse (BVP) and electromyographic activity (EDA). The data collected confirms a hypothesis based on three out of four criteria (engagement, music quality, coherency with game excitement, and coherency with performance) that players prefer dynamic affective music when asked to reflect on the current game-state. In the future this system could allow designers/composers to easily create affective and dynamic soundtracks for interactive applications.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, Marco","Togelius, Julian","Eklund, Peter","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S02-093.51-038376"],"event":{"acronym":"Audiomostly","end":"2018-09-14","place":"Wrexham, gb","start":"2018-09-12","title":"Audio Mostly 2018 on Sound in Immersion and Emotion","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deakin University","New York University"],"keyword":["Affective Dynamic Music","Evolutionary algorithms","Game related music experience","Hybrid Evolutionary Technique","MetaCompose","Music generation","Real time music generation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving in game mood expressive music with metacompose","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3243274.3243292","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.51-038376","identifier":[{"id":"85060905429","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c102e657-03e8-4f15-a55d-440db0a586e9","sdu-2d8a829b-ea18-4969-9f98-655d48d1947d"],"keyword":["Affective expression","Affective-dynamic music","Evolutionary algorithms","Game-related music experience","Hybrid evolutionary technique","MetaCompose","Music generation","Real-time music generation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-079C3B96E2777106E69116B07A878E31"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3243274.3243292","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83681336/scirea_am18.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Biorobotics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"deakin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Deakin University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","locid":"6e0315fe-6ee1-493f-a23d-7acc1c33cbcf","name":"Scirea, Marco","orcid":"0000-0003-4908-0526","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3243274.3243292","edition":"8","eisbn":["9781450366090"],"isbn":["9781450366090"],"place":"Wrexham, United Kingdom","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Audio Mostly","status":"p","title":"AM'18 Proceedings of the Audio Mostly 2018 on Sound in Immersion and Emotion","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060905429"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c102e657-03e8-4f15-a55d-440db0a586e9","sdu-2d8a829b-ea18-4969-9f98-655d48d1947d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Evolving in-game mood-expressive music with MetaCompose","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.51-038376","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Key to our project flora robotica is the idea of creating a bio-hybrid system of tightly coupled natural plants and distributed robots to grow architectural artifacts and spaces. Our motivation with this ground research project is to lay a principled foundation towards the design and implementation of living architectural systems that provide functionalities beyond those of orthodox building practice, such as self-repair, material accumulation and self-organization. Plants and robots work together to create a living organism that is inhabited by human beings. User-defined design objectives help to steer the directional growth of the plants, but also the system's interactions with its inhabitants determine locations where growth is prohibited or desired (e.g., partitions, windows, occupiable space). We report our plant species selection process and aspects of living architecture. A leitmotif of our project is the rich concept of braiding: braids are produced by robots from continuous material and serve as both scaffolds and initial architectural artifacts before plants take over and grow the desired architecture. We use light and hormones as attraction stimuli and far-red light as repelling stimulus to influence the plants. Applied sensors range from simple proximity sensing to detect the presence of plants to sophisticated sensing technology, such as electrophysiology and measurements of sap flow. We conclude by discussing our anticipated final demonstrator that integrates key features of flora robotica, such as the continuous growth process of architectural artifacts and self-repair of living architecture.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Divband Soorati, Mohammad","Heinrich, Mary Katherine","Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","Kuksin, Igor","Veenstra, Frank","Wahby, Mostafa","Nielsen, Stig Anton","Risi, Sebastian","Skrzypczak, Tomasz","Zahadat, Payam","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw","Støy, Kasper","Schmickl, Thomas","Kernbach, Serge","Ayres, Phil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-126277"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-04","place":"Lyon, fr","start":"2017-09-04","title":"Living Architectures Workshop 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica an architectural system combining living natural plants and distributed robots","src":["arkc"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.04291","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-126277","ids":["arkc-23766292-0a13-4a7c-85f6-d872d12b7052"],"keyword":["No"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DCD81E7B6B7AE9AFEF6564EB83A02550"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.04291","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"royal danish academy architecture design conservation","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-RDKA","l3nn":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation","namevar":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation, Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Institute of Architecture and Technology, CITA - Centre for Information Technology and Architecture","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation","The Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts, Schools of Architecture, Design and Conservation, School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-RDKA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"cybertronica ug","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"pl","key":"adam mickiewicz university","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Adam Mickiewicz University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Heiko","key":"hamannpau","last":"Hamann","name":"Hamann, Heiko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammad","key":"divbandsooratipau","last":"Divband Soorati","name":"Divband Soorati, Mohammad","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mary Katherine","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","locid":"08c85002-6341-40a3-9046-b6222a08f965","name":"Heinrich, Mary Katherine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Nicolas","key":"hofstadlerpau","last":"Hofstadler","name":"Hofstadler, Daniel Nicolas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Igor","key":"kuksinpau","last":"Kuksin","name":"Kuksin, Igor","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mostafa","key":"wahbypau","last":"Wahby","name":"Wahby, Mostafa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig Anton","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Stig Anton","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"skrzypczakpau","last":"Skrzypczak","name":"Skrzypczak, Tomasz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Payam","key":"zahadatpau","last":"Zahadat","name":"Zahadat, Payam","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Przemyslaw","key":"wojtaszekpau","last":"Wojtaszek","name":"Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","name":"Støy, Kasper","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"schmicklpau","last":"Schmickl","name":"Schmickl, Thomas","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Serge","key":"kernbachpau","last":"Kernbach","name":"Kernbach, Serge","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Phil","key":"ayrespau","last":"Ayres","locid":"809e3672-ddc8-44e7-8a1b-1c1309974305","name":"Ayres, Phil","orcid":"0000-0002-9266-065X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","subtitle":"the 14th European Conference on Artificial Life","title":"Proceedings of ECAL 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-23766292-0a13-4a7c-85f6-d872d12b7052"],"src":["Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Flora robotica -- An Architectural System Combining Living Natural Plants and Distributed Robots","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-126277","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary robots perform energy intensive tasks—e.g., manipulation and locomotion—making the development of energy autonomous robots challenging. Since plants are primary energy producers in natural ecosystems, we took plants as a source of inspiration for designing our robotics platform. This led us to investigate energy autonomy in robots through employing solar panels. As plants move slowly compared to other large terrestrial organisms, it is expected that plant-inspired robots can enable robotic applications, such as long-term monitoring and exploration, where energy consumption could be minimized. Since it is difficult to manually design robotic systems that adhere to full energy autonomy, we utilize evolutionary algorithms to automate the design and evaluation of energy harvesting robots. We demonstrate how artificial evolution can lead to the design and control of a modular plant-like robot. Robotic phenotypes were acquired through implementing an evolutionary algorithm, a generative encoding and modular building blocks in a simulation environment. The generative encoding is based on a context sensitive Lindenmayer-System (L-System) and the evolutionary algorithm is used to optimize compositions of heterogeneous modular building blocks in the simulation environment. Phenotypes that evolved from the simulation environment are in turn transferred to a physical robot platform. The robotics platform consists of five different types of modules: (1) a base module, (2) a cube module, (3) servo modules, and (4,5) two types of solar panel modules that are used to harvest energy. The control system for the platform is initially evolved in the simulation environment and afterward transferred to an actual physical robot. A few experiments were done showing the relationship between energy cost and the amount of light tracking that evolved in the simulation. The reconfigurable modular robots are eventually used to harvest light with the possibility to be reconfigured based on the needs of the designer, the type of usable modules, and/or the optimal configuration derived from the simulation environment. Long-term energy autonomy has not been tested in this robotics platform. However, we think our robotics platform can serve as a stepping stone toward full energy autonomy in modular robots.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Metayer, Chloe","Risi, Sebastian","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381465"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","IMT Mines Albi"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Energy autonomy","Evolutionary algorithms","Modular Robots","plant inspired robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"toward energy autonomy in heterogeneous modular plant inspired robots through artificial evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/frobt.2017.00043","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381465","identifier":[{"id":"85061993683","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0d455fa4-2b14-4126-8121-b78dba84a1cd"],"keyword":["artificial intelligence","energy autonomy","evolutionary algorithms","modular robots","plant-inspired robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2CF021C00A49DDB6FE21EBA801C4747"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/frobt.2017.00043","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82458405/veenstra_frontiers17_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"imt mines albi","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"IMT Mines Albi","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chloe","key":"metayerpau","last":"Metayer","name":"Metayer, Chloe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"stoypau","last":"Stoy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","name_org":"Stoy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/frobt.2017.00043","issn":["22969144"],"journal":"Frontiers in Robotics and AI","paperid":"43","publisher":"Frontiers","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Robotics and AI","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85061993683"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d455fa4-2b14-4126-8121-b78dba84a1cd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Toward energy Autonomy in heterogeneous Modular Plant-Inspired Robots through Artificial evolution","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381465","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes a work in progress on co-evolving Artificial Neural Networks (ANNs) for music improvisation. Using this neuro-evolutionary approach the ANNs adapt to the changes in the human player's music as input, while still maintaining some of the structure of the musical piece previously evolved. The system is called PRIMAL-IMPROV and evolves modules that are composed of two ANNs, one controlling pitch and one controlling rhythm. The results of a quantitative study show that, by only introducing simple rules as fitness functions, the system is able to generate more interesting arrangements than ANNs evolved without a specific objective. The emerging and interesting musical patterns that are produced by the evolved ANNs hint at the promising potential of the system.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, M.","Eklund, P.","Togelius, J.","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383357"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial neural networks","Evolutionary computation","Music","Network topology","Neural nets","Neural networks","PRIMAL IMPROV","Real time systems","Rhythm","Topology","co evolutionary musical improvisation","evolved ANN hint","human player","interesting musical patterns","music improvisation","neuro evolutionary approach"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"primal improv towards co evolutionary musical improvisation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456766/scirea_ceec17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383357","identifier":[{"id":"85040771181","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8e269b6d-006c-4d50-ac29-a01adec26089"],"keyword":["Network topology","Neural networks","PRIMAL-IMPROV","Real-time systems","Rhythm","Topology","artificial neural networks","co-evolutionary musical improvisation","evolutionary computation","evolved ANN hint","human player","interesting musical patterns","music","music improvisation","neural nets","neuro-evolutionary approach"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BAA64884D2429474547F45217D7ED609"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456766/scirea_ceec17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","name":"Scirea, M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","name_org":"Risi, S.","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ceec.2017.8101620","isbn":["9781538630075"],"pages":"172-177","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2017 9th Computer Science and Electronic Engineering (CEEC)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040771181"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8e269b6d-006c-4d50-ac29-a01adec26089"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Primal-improv: Towards co-evolutionary musical improvisation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383357","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a deep learning / neuroevolution hybrid approach called DLNE, which allows FPS bots to learn to aim & shoot based only on high-dimensional raw pixel input. The deep learning component is responsible for visual recognition and translating raw pixels to compact feature representations, while the evolving network takes those features as inputs to infer actions. The results suggest that combining deep learning and neuroevolution in a hybrid approach is a promising research direction that could make complex visual domains directly accessible to networks trained through evolution.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Poulsen, Andreas Precht","Thorhauge, Mark","Funch, Mikkel Hvilshj","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384593"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","FPS Bots","Hybrid approach","Neuroevolution","Visual Recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a deep learning neuroevolution hybrid for visual control","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457605/p93_precht_poulsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384593","ids":["itu-e1cf7480-2ebe-4fb4-8efc-4f828c2ef370"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","FPS Bots","Hybrid Approach","Neuroevolution","Visual Recognition"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-6B9EDA759E99B6E68D0BFD48D300116A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457605/p93_precht_poulsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Precht","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Andreas Precht","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"thorhaugepau","last":"Thorhauge","name":"Thorhauge, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Hvilshj","key":"funchpau","last":"Funch","name":"Funch, Mikkel Hvilshj","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3067695.3076016","isbn":["9781450349390"],"pages":"93-94","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GECCO '17 Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e1cf7480-2ebe-4fb4-8efc-4f828c2ef370"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A deep learning / neuroevolution hybrid for visual control","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384593","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Recent advances in 3D printing are revolutionizing manufacturing, enabling the fabrication of structures with unprecedented complexity and functionality. Yet biological systems are able to fabricate systems with far greater complexity using a process that involves assembling and folding a linear string. Here, we demonstrate a 1D printing system that uses an approach inspired by the ribosome to fabricate a variety of specialized robotic automata from a single string of source material. This proof-ofconcept system involves both a novel manufacturing platform that configures the source material using folding and a computational optimization tool that allows designs to be produced from the specification of high-level goals. We show that our 1D printing system is able to produce three distinct robots from the same source material, each of which is capable of accomplishing a specialized locomotion task. Moreover, we demonstrate the ability of the printer to use recycled material to produce new designs, enabling an autonomous manufacturing ecosystem capable of repurposing previous iterations to accomplish new tasks.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cellucci, Daniel","MacCurdy, Robert","Lipson, Hod","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381454"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","Cornell University","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Complexity theory","Printers","Robot kinematics","Three dimensional printing","Wires"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000001d printing of recyclable robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025742/cellucci_ral17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381454","identifier":[{"id":"85044032624","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0cab5497-6dd9-4914-ae70-353740cf5437"],"keyword":["Complexity theory","Printers","Robot kinematics","Three-dimensional printing","Wires"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FF401D640761E6FFF2773238A8DB894"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83025742/cellucci_ral17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"celluccipau","last":"Cellucci","name":"Cellucci, Daniel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"maccurdypau","last":"MacCurdy","name":"MacCurdy, Robert","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hod","key":"lipsonpau","last":"Lipson","name":"Lipson, Hod","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lra.2017.2716418","issn":["23773766"],"issue":"4","journal":"IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters","pages":"1964-1971","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Robotics and Automation Letters","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044032624"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0cab5497-6dd9-4914-ae70-353740cf5437"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"1D Printing of Recyclable Robots","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381454","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes an evaluation conducted on the MetaCompose music generator, which is based on evolutionary computation and uses a hybrid evolutionary technique that combines FI-2POP and multi-objective optimization. The main objective of MetaCompose is to create music in real-time that can express different mood-states. The experiment presented here aims to evaluate: (i) if the perceived mood experienced by the participants of a music score matches intended mood the system is trying to express and (ii) if participants can identify transitions in the mood expression that occur mid-piece. Music clips including transitions and with static affective states were produced by MetaCompose and a quantitative user study was performed. Participants were tasked with annotating the perceived mood and moreover were asked to annotate in real-time changes in valence. The data collected confirms the hypothesis that people can recognize changes in music mood and that MetaCompose can express perceptibly different levels of arousal. In regards to valence we observe that, while it is mainly perceived as expected, changes in arousal seems to also influence perceived valence, suggesting that one or more of the music features MetaCompose associates with arousal has some effect on valence as well.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, Marco","Eklund, Peter","Togelius, Julian","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382220"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","New York University"],"keyword":["affective computing music generation quantitative evaluation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can you feel it evaluation of affective expression in music generated by metacompose","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456585/scirea_gecco17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382220","identifier":[{"id":"85026380651","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-404e76e2-8ca4-491c-b27d-8b4a5823b8f6"],"keyword":["affective computing, music generation, quantitative evaluation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D8C29AAC50F0B8BF52B60A897B6248B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456585/scirea_gecco17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","name":"Scirea, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3071178.3071314","issn":["00010782","10591192"],"issn_org":["00010782"],"journal":"Communications of the ACM","pages":"211-218","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Communications of the ACM","title_org":"GECCO '17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026380651"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-404e76e2-8ca4-491c-b27d-8b4a5823b8f6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Can You Feel It?: Evaluation of Affective Expression in Music Generated by MetaCompose","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382220","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Training neural networks to quickly learn new skills without forgetting previously learned skills is an important open challenge in machine learning. A common problem for adaptive networks that can learn during their lifetime is that the weights encoding a particular task are often overridden when a new task is learned. This paper takes a step in overcoming this limitation by building on the recently proposed Evolving Neural Turing Machine (ENTM) approach. In the ENTM, neural networks are augmented with an external memory component that they can write to and read from, which allows them to store associations quickly and over long periods of time. The results in this paper demonstrate that the ENTM is able to perform one-shot learning in reinforcement learning tasks without catastrophic forgetting of previously stored associations. Additionally, we introduce a new ENTM default jump mechanism that makes it easier to find unused memory location and therefor facilitates the evolution of continual learning networks. Our results suggest that augmenting evolving networks with an external memory component is not only a viable mechanism for adaptive behaviors in neuroevolution but also allows these networks to perform continual and one-shot learning at the same time.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lüders, Benno","Schläger, Mikkel","Korach, Aleksandra","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383255"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Catastrophic Forgetting","Continual Learning","Evolving Neural Turing Machine ENTM","Neural networks","One Shot Learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continual and one shot learning through neural networks with dynamic external memory","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456686/lueders_evoapps17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383255","identifier":[{"id":"85017532406","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-87aa1065-c5e0-4d43-a073-579873be6d03"],"keyword":["Catastrophic Forgetting","Continual Learning","Evolving Neural Turing Machine (ENTM)","Neural Networks","One-Shot Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-41B806592D1A54E620CDFA1B9BAD4B0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456686/lueders_evoapps17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Benno","key":"lüderspau","last":"Lüders","name":"Lüders, Benno","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"schlägerpau","last":"Schläger","name":"Schläger, Mikkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandra","key":"korachpau","last":"Korach","name":"Korach, Aleksandra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-55849-3_57","eisbn":["9783319558493"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"886-901","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017532406"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-87aa1065-c5e0-4d43-a073-579873be6d03"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Continual and One-Shot Learning Through Neural Networks with Dynamic External Memory","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383255","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Evolutionary robotics is challenged with some key problems that must be solved, or at least mitigated extensively, before it can fulfill some of its promises to deliver highly autonomous and adaptive robots. The reality gap and the ability to transfer phenotypes from simulation to reality constitute one such problem. Another lies in the embodiment of the evolutionary processes, which links to the first, but focuses on how evolution can act on real agents and occur independently from simulation, that is, going from being, as Eiben et al. put it, “the evolution of things, rather than just the evolution of digital objects.…” The work presented here investigates how fully autonomous evolution of robot controllers can be realized in hardware, using an industrial robot and a marker-based computer vision system. In particular, this article presents an approach to automate the reconfiguration of the test environment and shows that it is possible, for the first time, to incrementally evolve a neural robot controller for different obstacle avoidance tasks with no human intervention. Importantly, the system offers a high level of robustness and precision that could potentially open up the range of problems amenable to embodied evolution.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Faina, Andres","Jacobsen, Lars Toft","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381543"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolution in hardware","Evolution of physical systems EPS","Evolutionary Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automating the incremental evolution of controllers for physical robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82003890/preprint_automating_incremental_evolution.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381543","identifier":[{"id":"85020057944","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-12778aa0-01a5-46ea-b984-17eecfa4fcb4"],"keyword":["Evolution of physical systems (EPS)","evolution in hardware","evolutionary robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-75559F1D68EE5051087507DFD993A61B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82003890/preprint_automating_incremental_evolution.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Toft","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Lars Toft","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/artl_a_00226","issn":["10645462","15309185"],"issn_org":["10645462"],"issue":"2","journal":"Artificial Life","pages":"142-168","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020057944"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-12778aa0-01a5-46ea-b984-17eecfa4fcb4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automating the Incremental Evolution of Controllers for Physical Robots","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381543","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We address the problem of playing turn-based multi-action adversarial games, which include many strategy games with extremely high branching factors as players take multiple actions each turn. This leads to the breakdown of standard tree search methods, including Monte Carlo Tree Search (MCTS), as they become unable to reach a sufficient depth in the game tree. In this paper, we introduce Online Evolutionary Planning (OEP) to address this challenge, which searches for combinations of actions to perform during a single turn guided by a fitness function that evaluates the quality of a particular state. We compare OEP to different MCTS variations that constrain the exploration to deal with the high branching factor in the turn-based multi-action game Hero Academy. While the constrained MCTS variations outperform the vanilla MCTS implementation by a large margin, OEP is able to search the space of plans more efficiently than any of the tested tree search methods as it has a relative advantage when the number of actions per turn increases.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Justesen, Niels","Mahlmann, Tobias","Risi, Sebastian","Togelius, Julian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383106"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","New York University"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Evolutionary computation","Monte Carlo tree search","Tree Search"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"playing multi action adversarial games online evolutionary planning versus tree search","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456662/justesen_tciaig17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383106","identifier":[{"id":"85029148021","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7db68d4d-c0c0-4055-87d5-1e6dc179797e"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Monte Carlo tree search","evolutionary computation","tree search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B758AB4AB4FC61C54D61404EA6277791"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456662/justesen_tciaig17.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"justesenpau","last":"Justesen","name":"Justesen, Niels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"mahlmannpau","last":"Mahlmann","name":"Mahlmann, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tciaig.2017.2738156","issn":["1943068X","19430698"],"issn_org":["1943068X"],"journal":"IEEE Transactions on Computational Intelligence and AI in Games","pages":"281-291","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Computational Intelligence and AI in Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087797993"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7db68d4d-c0c0-4055-87d5-1e6dc179797e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Playing Multi-Action Adversarial Games: Online Evolutionary Planning versus Tree Search","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383106","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes the MetaCompose music generator, a compositional, extensible framework for affective music composition. In this context ‘affective’ refers to the music generator’s ability to express emotional information. The main purpose of MetaCompose is to create music in real-time that can express different mood-states, which we achieve through a unique combination of a graph traversal-based chord sequence generator, a search-based melody generator, a pattern-based accompaniment generator, and a theory for mood expression. Melody generation uses a novel evolutionary technique combining FI-2POP with multi-objective optimization. This allows us to explore a Pareto front of diverse solutions that are creatively equivalent under the terms of a multi-criteria objective function. Two quantitative user studies were performed to evaluate the system: one focusing on the music generation technique, and the other that explores valence expression, via the introduction of dissonances. The results of these studies demonstrate (i) that each part of the generation system improves the perceived quality of the music produced, and (ii) how valence expression via dissonance produces the perceived affective state. This system, which can reliably generate affect-expressive music, can subsequently be integrated in any kind of interactive application (e.g., games) to create an adaptive and dynamic soundtrack.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, Marco","Togelius, Julian","Eklund, Peter","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384836"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","New York University"],"keyword":["Affective music","Creative computing","Evolutionary computing","Genetic algorithm","Music generation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"affective evolutionary music composition with metacompose","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82428771/metacompose_journal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384836","identifier":[{"id":"85020633618","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f2a6c343-3a4a-4e23-a2e5-85a722ad83f7"],"keyword":["Affective music","Creative computing","Evolutionary computing","Genetic algorithm","Music generation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-713712713D91B1318633B3174159D9AA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://marcoscirea.com/papers/metacompose-journal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82428771/metacompose_journal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","name":"Scirea, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10710-017-9307-y","issn":["13892576","15737632"],"issn_org":["13892576"],"journal":"Genetic Programming and Evolvable Machines","pages":"1-33","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Genetic Programming and Evolvable Machines"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020633618"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f2a6c343-3a4a-4e23-a2e5-85a722ad83f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Affective evolutionary music composition with MetaCompose","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384836","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The real-time strategy game StarCraft has become an important benchmark for AI research as it poses a complex environment with numerous challenges. An important strategic aspect in this game is to decide what buildings and units to produce. StarCraft bots playing in AI competitions today are only able to switch between predefined strategies, which makes it hard to adapt to new situations. This paper introduces an evolutionary-based method to overcome this challenge, called Continual Online Evolutionary Planning (COEP), which is able to perform in-game adaptive build-order planning. COEP was added to an open source StarCraft bot called UAlbertaBot and is able to outperform the built-in bots in the game as well as being competitive against a number of scripted opening strategies. The COEP augmented bot can change its build order dynamically and quickly adapt to the opponent’s strategy.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Justesen, Niels Orsleff","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381484"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary Planning","StarCraft","adaptive AI","build order optimization","real time strategy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continual online evolutionary planning for in game build order adaptation in starcraft","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81965010/justesen_gecco17.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381484","identifier":[{"id":"85026384177","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0ea9a6be-d106-46bd-8d1c-de77b358f870"],"keyword":["StarCraft","adaptive AI","build-order optimization","evolutionary planning","real-time strategy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AD3E75491BEA5927A9A419ADB40BAEB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81965010/justesen_gecco17.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Orsleff","key":"justesenpau","last":"Justesen","name":"Justesen, Niels Orsleff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3071178.3071210","isbn":["9781450349208"],"pages":"187-194","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GECCO ’17 Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026384177"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0ea9a6be-d106-46bd-8d1c-de77b358f870"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Continual Online Evolutionary Planning for In-Game Build Order Adaptation in StarCraft","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381484","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Human-based computation (HBC) is an emerging research area in which humans and machines collaborate to solve tasks that neither one can solve in isolation. In evolutionary computation, HBC is often realized through interactive evolutionary computation (IEC), in which a user guides evolution by iteratively selecting the parents for the next generation. IEC has shown promise in a variety of different domains, but evolving more complex or hierarchically composed behaviours remains challenging with the traditional IEC approach. To overcome this challenge, this paper combines the recently introduced ESP (encapsulation, syllabus and pandemonium) algorithm with IEC to allow users to intuitively break complex challenges into smaller pieces and preserve, reuse and combine interactively evolved sub-skills. The combination of ESP principles with IEC provides a new way in which human insights can be leveraged in evolutionary computation and, as the results in this paper show, IEC-ESP is able to solve complex control problems that are challenging for a traditional fitness-based approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["González de Prado Salas, Pablo","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383845"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","title":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ESP algorithm","Evolutionary control problems","Hierarchical task decomposition","Human based computation","Interactive evolutionary computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive evolution of complex behaviours through skill encapsulation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82351742/GonzalezDePradoSalas.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383845","identifier":[{"id":"85017541047","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b0bdf893-fe84-4b22-b2c9-5f66a9334637"],"keyword":["ESP algorithm","Evolutionary control problems","Hierarchical task decomposition","Human-based computation","Interactive evolutionary computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CD15093A2F6F54714FD6FC0107AF878B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B_kxyTDDOMQJZVpvdW1iNzl6SlU/view","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82351742/GonzalezDePradoSalas.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pablo","key":"gonzálezdepradosalaspau","last":"González de Prado Salas","name":"González de Prado Salas, Pablo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Giovanni","key":"squilleropedh","last":"Squillero","name":"Squillero, Giovanni","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kevin","key":"simpedh","last":"Sim","name":"Sim, Kevin","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-55849-3_55","eisbn":["9783319558493"],"isbn":["9783319558486"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"853-869","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"European Conference on the Applications of Evolutionary Computation","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation. EvoApplications 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017541047"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b0bdf893-fe84-4b22-b2c9-5f66a9334637"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive Evolution of Complex Behaviours Through Skill Encapsulation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383845","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384612"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving simulated modular robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82063888/evolving_simulated_modular_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384612","ids":["itu-e2ffe95a-13e7-4f08-953f-1ab046df2343"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-208C249102894E0C102E06D0723BE104"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82063888/evolving_simulated_modular_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e2ffe95a-13e7-4f08-953f-1ab046df2343"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving Simulated Modular Robots","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384612","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Modular robots oer an important benet in evolutionary robotics, which is to quickly evaluate evolved morphologies and control systems in reality. However, articial evolution of simulated modular robotics is a dicult and time consuming task requiring signicant computational power. While articial evolution in virtual creatures has made use of powerful generative encodings, here we investigate how a generative encoding and direct encoding compare for the evolution of locomotion in modular robots when the number of robotic modules changes. Simulating less modules would decrease the size of the genome of a direct encoding while the size of the genome of the implemented generative encoding stays the same. We found that the generative encoding is signi cantly more ecient in creating robot phenotypes in the initial stages of evolution when simulating a maximum of 5, 10, and 20 modules. This not only conrms that generative encodings lead to decent performance more quickly, but also that when simulating just a few modules a generative encoding is more powerful than a direct encoding for creating robotic structures. Over longer evolutionary time, the dierence between the encodings no longer becomes statistically signicant. This leads us to speculate that a combined approach { starting with a generative encoding and later implementing a direct encoding { can lead to more ecient evolved designs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Risi, Sebastian","Støy, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382184"],"event":{"acronym":"EvoApplications","end":"2017-04-21","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2017-04-19","title":"Evostar 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Direct Generative Encodings","Evolutionary algorithms","Modular Robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolution and morphogenesis of simulated modular robots a comparison between a direct and generative encoding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81921390/Veenstra2017_EvolutionAndMorphogenesisofSimulatedModularRobots.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382184","identifier":[{"id":"85017551035","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3e05d80f-13ca-438f-8722-697a1beda810"],"keyword":["Direct & Generative Encodings","Evolutionary Algorithms","Modular Robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F7119E100722104C4A9A7E083622E1A9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81921390/Veenstra2017_EvolutionAndMorphogenesisofSimulatedModularRobots.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-55849-3_56","eisbn":["9783319558493"],"isbn":["9783319558486"],"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th European Conference, EvoApplications 2017, Amsterdam, The Netherlands, April 19-21, 2017, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Applications of Evolutionary Computation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017551035"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3e05d80f-13ca-438f-8722-697a1beda810"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolution and Morphogenesis of Simulated Modular Robots: A Comparison Between a Direct and Generative Encoding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382184","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper investigates the potential of combining deep learning and neuroevolution to create a bot for a simple first person shooter (FPS) game capable of aiming and shooting based on high-dimensional raw pixel input. The deep learning component is responsible for visual recognition and translating raw pixels to compact feature representations, while the evolving network takes those features as inputs to infer actions. Two types of feature representations are evaluated in terms of (1) how precise they allow the deep network to recognize the position of the enemy, (2) their effect on evolution, and (3) how well they allow the deep network and evolved network to interface with each other. Overall, the results suggest that combining deep learning and neuroevolution in a hybrid approach is a promising research direction that could make complex visual domains directly accessible to networks trained through evolution.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Poulsen, Andreas Precht","Thorhauge, Mark","Funch, Mikkel Hvilshj","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382209"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deep learning","Feature Representations","First Person Shooter FPS","Neuroevolution","Visual Recognition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dlne a hybridization of deep learning and neuroevolution for visual control","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456643/poulsen_cig17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382209","identifier":[{"id":"85039990726","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3fbb5366-9e64-4056-890e-caef3213113d"],"keyword":["Deep Learning","Feature Representations","First Person Shooter (FPS)","Neuroevolution","Visual Recognition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02138D8D02327E7FFD50926293A67BCD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456643/poulsen_cig17_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Precht","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Andreas Precht","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"thorhaugepau","last":"Thorhauge","name":"Thorhauge, Mark","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Hvilshj","key":"funchpau","last":"Funch","name":"Funch, Mikkel Hvilshj","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2017.8080444","eisbn":["9781538632338"],"pages":"256-263","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence and Games (CIG), 2017 IEEE Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85039990726"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3fbb5366-9e64-4056-890e-caef3213113d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DLNE: A hybridization of deep learning and neuroevolution for visual control","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382209","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The real-time strategy game StarCraft has proven to be a challenging environment for artificial intelligence techniques, and as a result, current state-of-the-art solutions consist of numerous hand-crafted modules. In this paper, we show how macromanagement decisions in StarCraft can be learned directly from game replays using deep learning. Neural networks are trained on 789,571 state-action pairs extracted from 2,005 replays of highly skilled players, achieving top-1 and top-3 error rates of 54.6% and 22.9% in predicting the next build action. By integrating the trained network into UAlbertaBot, an open source StarCraft bot, the system can significantly outperform the game’s built-in Terran bot, and play competitively against UAlbertaBot with a fixed rush strategy. To our knowledge, this is the first time macromanagement tasks are learned directly from replays in StarCraft. While the best hand-crafted strategies are still the state-of-the-art, the deep network approach is able to express a wide range of different strategies and thus improving the network’s performance further with deep reinforcement learning is an immediately promising avenue for future research. Ultimately this approach could lead to strong StarCraft bots that are less reliant on hard-coded strategies.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Justesen, Niels","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382911"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Deep learning","Neural networks","Real time strategy games","StarCraft macromanagement"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning macromanagement in starcraft from replays using deep learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456707/njustesen2017learning.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382911","identifier":[{"id":"85040008192","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6e7acde3-44fa-4be0-985f-cd20893638f7"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Deep learning","Neural networks","Real-time strategy games","StarCraft macromanagement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C2FFF207EAE4FA13F88BDF9C30280E1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456707/njustesen2017learning.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"justesenpau","last":"Justesen","name":"Justesen, Niels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2017.8080430","isbn":["9781538632338"],"pages":"162-169","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence and Games (CIG), 2017 IEEE Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040008192"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6e7acde3-44fa-4be0-985f-cd20893638f7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Learning macromanagement in starcraft from replays using deep learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382911","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Cellular Automata (CA) are a remarkable example of morphogenetic system, where cells grow and self-organise through local interactions. CA have been used as abstractions of biological development and artificial life. Such systems have been able to show properties that are often desirable but difficult to achieve in engineered systems, e.g. morphogenesis and replication of regular patterns without any form of centralized coordination. However, cellular systems are hard to program (i.e. evolve) and control, especially when the number of cell states and neighbourhood increase. In this paper, we propose a new principle of morphogenesis based on Compositional Pattern Producing Networks (CPPNs), an abstraction of development that has been able to produce complex structural motifs without local interactions. CPPNs are used as Cellular Automata genotypes and evolved with a NeuroEvolution of Augmenting Topologies (NEAT) algorithm. This allows complexification of genomes throughout evolution with phenotypes emerging from self-organisation through development based on local interactions. In this paper, the problems of 2D pattern morphogenesis and replication are investigated. Results show that CA-NEAT is an appropriate means of approaching cellular systems engineering, especially for future applications where natural levels of complexity are targeted. We argue that CA-NEAT could provide a valuable mapping for morphogenetic systems, beyond cellular automata systems, where development through local interactions is desired.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nichele, Stefano","Ose, Mathias Berild","Risi, Sebastian","Tufte, Gunnar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384490"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences"],"keyword":["Artificial Life","Cellular automata","Compositional Pattern Producing Network CPPN","EvoDevo","NeuroEvolution of Augmenting Topologies NEAT"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ca neat evolved compositional pattern producing networks for cellular automata morphogenesis and replication","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456613/nichele_tcds2017_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384490","identifier":[{"id":"85028466695","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-db6a6aa7-866e-4a70-835d-38dc5b21fd4e"],"keyword":["Artificial Life","Cellular Automata","Compositional Pattern Producing Network (CPPN)","EvoDevo","NeuroEvolution of Augmenting Topologies (NEAT)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2E3015C692AB800732BC8973AFB31DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82456613/nichele_tcds2017_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"oslo and akershus university college of applied sciences","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Oslo and Akershus University College of Applied Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefano","key":"nichelepau","last":"Nichele","name":"Nichele, Stefano","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Berild","key":"osepau","last":"Ose","name":"Ose, Mathias Berild","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunnar","key":"tuftepau","last":"Tufte","name":"Tufte, Gunnar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tcds.2017.2737082","issn":["23798920","23798939"],"journal":"IEEE Transactions on Cognitive and Developmental Systems","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Cognitive and Developmental Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028466695"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-db6a6aa7-866e-4a70-835d-38dc5b21fd4e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CA-NEAT: Evolved Compositional Pattern Producing Networks for Cellular Automata Morphogenesis and Replication","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384490","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents first results from an interdisciplinary project, in which the fields of architecture, philosophy and artificial life are combined to explore possible futures of architecture. Through an interactive evolutionary installation, called EvoCurtain, we investigate aspects of how living in the future could occur, if built spaces could evolve and adapt alongside inhabitants. As such, present study explores the interdisciplinary possibilities in utilizing computational power to co-create with users and generate designs based on human input. We argue that this could lead to the development of designs tailored to the individual preferences of inhabitants, changing the roles of architects and designers entirely. Architecture-as-it-could-be is a philosophical approach conducted through artistic methods to anticipate the technological futures of human-centered development within architect.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bak, Sebastian HOlt","Rask, Nina","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381941"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Architecture Artificial life Evolutionary computation Interactive evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards adaptive evolutionary architecture","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-31008-4_4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381941","identifier":[{"id":"84962485867","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2d90d17f-26a3-4009-8545-6d9bb19694a1"],"keyword":["Architecture, Artificial life, Evolutionary computation, Interactive evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32D90DB2F38677AFE44A9069B30487B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82419454/bak_evomusart16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-31008-4_4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-31008-4_4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian HOlt","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","name":"Bak, Sebastian HOlt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","name":"Rask, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-31008-4_4","eisbn":["9783319310084"],"isbn":["9783319310077"],"issn":["16175468"],"pages":"47-62","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Informatics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 5th International Conference on Evolutionary and Biologically Inspired Music, Sound, Art and Design - Volume 9596"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962485867"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2d90d17f-26a3-4009-8545-6d9bb19694a1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Adaptive Evolutionary Architecture","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381941","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
