{"abstract":"Continual learning, i.e. the ability to sequentially learn tasks without catastrophic forgetting of previously learned ones, is an important open challenge in machine learning. In this paper we take a step in this direction by showing that the recently proposed Evolving Neural Turing Machine (ENTM) approach is able to perform one-shot learning in a reinforcement learning task without catastrophic forgetting of previously stored associations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lüders, Benno","Schläger, Mikkel","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384109"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Catastrophic Forgetting","Continual Learning","Evolving Neural Turing Machine","One Shot Learning","Reinforcement learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"continual learning through evolvable neural turing machines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81961428/CLDL_2016_paper_9.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384109","ids":["itu-c280bad8-f75b-4410-bdb2-f8c102d7ff85"],"keyword":["Catastrophic forgetting","Continual learning","Evolving Neural Turing Machine","One-shot learning","Reinforcement learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-91C98956069DC5EE6D5A2E6A0A8BE2C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81961428/CLDL_2016_paper_9.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://sites.google.com/site/cldlnips2016/submissions","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Benno","key":"lüderspau","last":"Lüders","name":"Lüders, Benno","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"schlägerpau","last":"Schläger","name":"Schläger, Mikkel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c280bad8-f75b-4410-bdb2-f8c102d7ff85"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Continual Learning through Evolvable Neural Turing Machines","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384109","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes a compositional, extensible framework for music composition and a user study to systematically evaluate its core components. These components include a graph traversal-based chord sequence generator, a search-based melody generator and a pattern-based accompaniment generator. An important contribution of this paper is the melody generator which uses a novel evolutionary technique combining FI-2POP and multi-objective optimization. A participant-based evaluation overwhelmingly confirms that all current components of the framework combine effectively to create harmonious, pleasant and interesting compositions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Scirea, Marco","Togelius, Julian","Eklund, Peter","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382904"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Compositional Framework","Evolutionary Technique","Graph Traversal Based Generator","Multi objective optimization","Music Composition"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metacompose a compositional evolutionary music composer","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82418836/scirea_evomusart16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382904","identifier":[{"id":"84962573454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6df4339b-5b69-49ae-bb27-739e41df615b"],"keyword":["Compositional Framework","Evolutionary Technique","Graph Traversal-Based Generator","Multi-Objective Optimization","Music Composition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C59034EEE94656B88921EE89DE7A4462"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82418836/scirea_evomusart16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"scireapau","last":"Scirea","name":"Scirea, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, Julian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"eklundpau","last":"Eklund","name":"Eklund, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-31008-4_14","eisbn":["9783319310084"],"isbn":["9783319310077"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"202-217","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"5th International Conference, EvoMUSART 2016, Porto, Portugal, March 30 -- April 1, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Evolutionary and Biologically Inspired Music, Sound, Art and Design"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84962573454"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6df4339b-5b69-49ae-bb27-739e41df615b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MetaCompose: A Compositional Evolutionary Music Composer","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382904","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Advances in supervised learning with deep neural networks have enabled robust classification in many real world domains. An interesting question is if such advances can also be leveraged effectively for computational creativity. One insight is that because evolutionary algorithms are free from strict requirements of mathematical smoothness, they can exploit powerful deep learning representations through arbitrary computational pipelines. In this way, deep networks trained on typical supervised tasks can be used as an ingredient in an evolutionary algorithm driven towards creativity. To highlight such potential, this paper creates novel 3D objects by leveraging feedback from a deep network trained only to recognize 2D images. This idea is tested by extending previous work with Innovation Engines, i.e. a principled combination of deep learning and evolutionary algorithms for computational creativity. The results of this automated process are interesting and recognizable 3D-printable objects, demonstrating the creative potential for combining evolutionary computation and deep learning in this way.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lehman, Joel Anthony","Risi, Sebastian","Clune, Jeff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384409"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-01","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2016-06-27","title":"International Conference on Computational Creativity","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D Object Generation","Computational Creativity","Deep neural networks","Evolutionary algorithms","Supervised learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creative generation of 000000000003d objects with deep learning and innovation engines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.computationalcreativity.net/iccc2016/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Proceedings_ICCC16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384409","identifier":[{"id":"85085261258","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d5ca2ebb-25dc-495c-a167-554c51a8b7ea"],"keyword":["3D Object Generation","Computational Creativity","Deep Neural Networks","Evolutionary Algorithms","Supervised Learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-48E42C7BB02F98BD4D08E3F9E4D0350E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.computationalcreativity.net/iccc2016/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/Proceedings_ICCC16.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebastianrisi.com/wp-content/uploads/lehman_iccc2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82428788/lehman_iccc2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, TiP and Games Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joel Anthony","key":"lehmanpau","last":"Lehman","name":"Lehman, Joel Anthony","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeff","key":"clunepau","last":"Clune","name":"Clune, Jeff","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9782746691551"],"isbn":["9782746691551"],"pages":"180-187","publisher":"Sony CSL Paris","status":"p","subtitle":"ICCC 2016","title":"Proceedings of the Seventh International Conference on Computational Creativity"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085261258"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d5ca2ebb-25dc-495c-a167-554c51a8b7ea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Creative Generation of 3D Objects with Deep Learning and Innovation Engines","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384409","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Creating controllers for NPCs in video games is traditionally a challenging and time consuming task. Automated learning methods such as neuroevolution (i.e. evolving artificial neural networks) have shown promise in this context but they often require carefully designed fitness functions to encourage the evolution of desired behaviors. In this paper, we show how casual users can create controllers for \\emph{Super Mario Bros} through an interactive evolutionary computation (IEC) approach, without prior domain or programming knowledge. By iteratively selecting Super Mario behaviors from a set of candidates, users are able to guide evolution towards a variety of different behaviors, which would be difficult with an automated approach. Additionally, the user-evolved controllers perform similarly well as controllers evolved with a traditional fitness-based approach when comparing distance traveled. The results suggest that IEC is a viable alternative in designing complex controllers for video games that could be extended to other games in the future.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Patrikk D.","Olsen, Jeppeh M.","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384923"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["game ai interactive evolution neuroevolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive super mario bros evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84986294108","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384923","identifier":[{"id":"84986294108","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f84f0637-49a7-4072-b2b9-ec39b33777c9"],"keyword":["game ai, interactive evolution, neuroevolution"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2F80B860BD9D898A8FECC536182368E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrikk D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Patrikk D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppeh M.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jeppeh M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908961.2908997","isbn":["9781450343237"],"pages":"41-42","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84986294108"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f84f0637-49a7-4072-b2b9-ec39b33777c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive Super Mario Bros Evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384923","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Creating controllers for NPCs in video games is traditionally a challenging and time consuming task. While automated learning methods such as neuroevolution (i.e. evolving artificial neural networks) have shown promise in this context, they often still require carefully designed fitness functions. In this paper, we show how casual users can create controllers for Super Mario Bros. through an interactive evolutionary computation (IEC) approach, without prior domain or programming knowledge. By iteratively selecting Super Mario behaviors from a set of candidates, users are able to guide evolution towards behaviors they prefer. The result of a user test show that the participants are able to evolve controllers with very diverse behaviors, which would be difficult through automated approaches. Additionally, the user-evolved controllers perform as well as controllers evolved with a traditional fitness-based approach in terms of distance traveled. The results suggest that IEC is a viable alternative in designing diverse controllers for video games that could be extended to other games in the future.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sørensen, Patrikk D.","Olsen, Jeppeh M.","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381907"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interactive evolutionary computation","NPC Controllers","Neuroevolution","User Guided Evolution","Video games"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"breeding a diversity of super mario behaviors through interactive evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.ntua.gr/IEEE_CIG16_Full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381907","identifier":[{"id":"85015417658","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2b4d2200-93f9-4295-9ce9-8a948bbf0e7f"],"keyword":["Interactive Evolutionary Computation","NPC Controllers","Neuroevolution","User-Guided Evolution","Video Games"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D1FF0061F14C95238006BE3D70181E06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.ntua.gr/IEEE_CIG16_Full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sebastianrisi.com/wp-content/uploads/sorensen_cig16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrikk D.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Patrikk D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppeh M.","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Jeppeh M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"357-363","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2b4d2200-93f9-4295-9ce9-8a948bbf0e7f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Breeding a Diversity of Super Mario Behaviors Through Interactive Evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381907","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Procedural content generation has shown promise in a variety of different games. In this paper we introduce a new kind of game, called Artefacts, that combines a sandbox-like environment akin to Minecraft with the ability to interactively evolve unique three-dimensional building blocks. Artefacts does not only allow players to collaborate by building larger structures from evolved objects but also to continue evolution of others’ artefacts. Results from playtests on three different game iterations indicate that players generally enjoy playing the game and are able to discover a wide variety of different 3D objects. Morever, while there is no explicit goal in Artefacts, the sandbox environment together with the ability to evolve unique shapes does allow for some interesting gameplay to emerge.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Patrascu, Cristinel","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382958"],"event":{"acronym":"CIG","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["3D Object Evolution","Collaborative Gameplay","Emergent Gameplay","Procedural Content Generation","Sandbox Games"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"artefacts minecraft meets collaborative interactive evolution","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.ntua.gr/IEEE_CIG16_Full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382958","identifier":[{"id":"85015448308","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-72400865-c1ca-40f8-8c7e-89ba845e4286"],"keyword":["3D Object Evolution","Collaborative Gameplay","Emergent Gameplay","Procedural Content Generation","Sandbox Games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CD9316769F75C10E3D94E01011EB2FE1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81843661/patrascu_cig16.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://image.ntua.gr/IEEE_CIG16_Full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Cristinel","key":"patrascupau","last":"Patrascu","name":"Patrascu, Cristinel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"349-356","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence and Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-72400865-c1ca-40f8-8c7e-89ba845e4286"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Artefacts: Minecraft meets Collaborative Interactive Evolution","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382958","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Neuroevolution (i.e. evolving artificial neural networks (ANNs) through evolutionary algorithms) has shown promise in evolving agents and robot controllers, which display complex behaviours and can adapt to their environments. These properties are also relevant to video games, since they can increase their longevity and replayability. However, the design of most current games precludes the use of any techniques which might yield unpredictable or even open-ended results. This article describes the game EvoCommander, with the goal to further demonstrate the potential of neuroevolution in games. In EvoCommander the player incrementally evolves an arsenal of ANN-controlled behaviors (e.g. ranged attack, flee, etc.) for a simple robot that has to battle other player and computer controlled robots. The game introduces the novel game mechanic of “brain switching”, selecting which evolved neural network is active at any point during battle. Results from playtests indicate that brain switching is a promising new game mechanic, leading to players employing interesting different strategies when training their robots and when controlling them in battle.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jallov, D.","Risi, Sebastian","Togelius, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383565"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Biological neural networks","Games","Robots","Switches","Training","Weapons"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evocommander a novel game based on evolving and switching between artificial brains","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82367846/Jallov2016EvoCommander.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383565","identifier":[{"id":"85026755974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9d575104-b465-4923-bd5b-e59838b893b0"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Biological neural networks","Games","Robots","Switches","Training","Weapons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16A24CEE8D83E3F1FF3FBB31F93A090D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82367846/Jallov2016EvoCommander.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"jallovpau","last":"Jallov","name":"Jallov, D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","name_org":"Risi, S.","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"togeliuspau","last":"Togelius","name":"Togelius, J.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tciaig.2016.2535416","issn":["1943068X","19430698"],"issn_org":["1943068X"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Computational Intelligence and AI in Games","pages":"181-191","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Computational Intelligence and AI in Games","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026755974"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9d575104-b465-4923-bd5b-e59838b893b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EvoCommander: A Novel Game Based on Evolving and Switching Between Artificial Brains","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383565","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Due to the replacement of natural flora and fauna with ur- ban environments, a significant part of the earth’s organisms that function as primary consumers have been dispelled. To compensate for the reduction in the amount of primary con- sumers, robotic systems that mimic plant-like organisms are interesting to mimic for their potential functional and aes- thetic value in urban environments. To investigate how to utilize plant developmental strategies in order to engender ur- ban artificial plants, we built a simple evolutionary model that applies an L-System based grammar as an abstraction of plant development. In the presented experiments, phytomorpholo- gies (plant morphologies) are iteratively constructed using a context sensitive L-System. The genomic representation of the L-System is subject to mutation by an evolutionary al- gorithm. These mutations thus alter the developmental rules of these phytomorphologies. We compare the differences be- tween the light absorption of evolving virtual plants that re- main static during their life and virtual plants that possess the possibility to move joints that link the separate parts of the virtual plants. Our results show that our evolutionary al- gorithm did not exploit potential beneficial joint actuation, instead, mostly static structures evolved. The results of our evolving L-System show that it is able to create various phy- tomorphologies, albeit that the results are preliminary and will be more thoroughly investigated in the future","author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382007"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-08","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2016-07-04","title":"Artificial Life","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","L Systems","Plant Inspired Robotics","Simulated Evolution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"generating artificial plant morphologies for function and aesthetics through evolving l systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81213335/Eventual_article_Plant.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382007","identifier":[{"id":"85087106895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-32dfa560-6838-4b38-8c1f-ccd0a0fcb432"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Robotics","L-Systems","Plant-Inspired Robotics","Simulated Evolution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-496139302AC1F596981041A15F298CCB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81213335/Eventual_article_Plant.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9780262339360"],"pages":"692-699","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Artificial Life Conference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087106895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-32dfa560-6838-4b38-8c1f-ccd0a0fcb432"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Generating Artificial Plant Morphologies for Function and Aesthetics through Evolving L-Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382007","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We present a survey of the first 21 years of web-based artificial life (WebAL) research and applications, broadly construed to include the many different ways in which artificial life and web technologies might intersect. Our survey covers the period from 1994—when the first WebAL work appeared—up to the present day, together with a brief discussion of relevant precursors. We examine recent projects, from 2010–2015, in greater detail in order to highlight the current state of the art. We follow the survey with a discussion of common themes and methodologies that can be observed in recent work and identify a number of likely directions for future work in this exciting area.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Taylor, Tim","Auerbach, Joshua E","Bongard, Josh","Clune, Jeff","Hickinbotham, Simon","Ofria, Charles","Oka, Mizuki","Risi, Sebastian","Stanley, Kenneth O","Yosinski, Jason"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383005"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Crowdfunding","Crowdsourcing","HTML5","Open science","Public outreach","Web technologies","WebAL"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"webal comes of age a review of the first 000000000021 years of artificial life on the web","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/ARTL_a_00211","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383005","identifier":[{"id":"84982245292","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-75d0f261-8a97-4279-acdb-d0d8d168a816"],"keyword":["HTML5","WebAL","crowdfunding","crowdsourcing","open science","public outreach","web technologies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-00891A11E9252DE51E405DC6568A1CBD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1162/ARTL_a_00211","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82422305/taylor_webal_artl_published.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mitpressjournals.org/doi/pdf/10.1162/ARTL_a_00211","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Tim","key":"taylorpau","last":"Taylor","name":"Taylor, Tim","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joshua E","key":"auerbachpau","last":"Auerbach","name":"Auerbach, Joshua E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Josh","key":"bongardpau","last":"Bongard","name":"Bongard, Josh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeff","key":"clunepau","last":"Clune","name":"Clune, Jeff","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"hickinbothampau","last":"Hickinbotham","name":"Hickinbotham, Simon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles","key":"ofriapau","last":"Ofria","name":"Ofria, Charles","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mizuki","key":"okapau","last":"Oka","name":"Oka, Mizuki","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth O","key":"stanleypau","last":"Stanley","name":"Stanley, Kenneth O","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jason","key":"yosinskipau","last":"Yosinski","name":"Yosinski, Jason","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1162/artl_a_00211","issn":["10645462","15309185"],"issn_org":["10645462"],"issue":"3","journal":"Artificial Life","pages":"364-407","publisher":"MIT Press","status":"p","title":"Artificial Life","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982245292"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-75d0f261-8a97-4279-acdb-d0d8d168a816"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"WebAL Comes of Age: A review of the first 21 years of Artificial Life on the Web","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383005","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"An important challenge in neuroevolution is to evolve multimodal behavior. Indirect network encodings can potentially answer this challenge. Yet in practice, indirect encodings do not yield effective multimodal controllers. This paper introduces novel multimodal extensions to HyperNEAT, a popular indirect encoding. A previous multimodal approach called situational policy geometry assumes that multiple brains benefit from being embedded within an explicit geometric space. However, this paper introduces HyperNEAT extensions for evolving many brains without assuming geometric relationships between them. The resulting Multi-Brain HyperNEAT can exploit human-specified task divisions, or can automatically discover when brains should be used, and how many to use. Experiments show that multi-brain approaches are more effective than HyperNEAT without multimodal extensions, and that brains without a geometric relation to each other are superior.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schrum, Jacob","Lehman, Joel","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383300"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["indirect encoding modularity multimodal behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"automatic evolution of multimodal behavior with multi brain hyperneat","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84986243147","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383300","identifier":[{"id":"84986243147","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8b021795-3a89-41c2-a74e-7177060e2393"],"keyword":["indirect encoding, modularity, multimodal behavior"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FA3A5BA609709BA4034B9ED216B3B72E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"schrumpau","last":"Schrum","name":"Schrum, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joel","key":"lehmanpau","last":"Lehman","name":"Lehman, Joel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908961.2908965","isbn":["9781450343237"],"pages":"21-22","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 on Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84986243147"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8b021795-3a89-41c2-a74e-7177060e2393"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Automatic Evolution of Multimodal Behavior with Multi-Brain HyperNEAT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383300","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"An unsolved problem in neuroevolution (NE) is to evolve artificial neural networks (ANN) that can store and use information to change their behavior online. While plastic neural networks have shown promise in this context, they have difficulties retaining information over longer periods of time and integrating new information without losing previously acquired skills. Here we build on recent work by Graves et al. [5] who extended the capabilities of an ANN by combining it with an external memory bank trained through gradient descent. In this paper, we introduce an evolvable version of their Neural Turing Machine (NTM) and show that such an approach greatly simplifies the neural model, generalizes better, and does not require accessing the entire memory content at each time-step. The Evolvable Neural Turing Machine (ENTM) is able to solve a simple copy tasks and for the first time, the continuous version of the double T-Maze, a complex reinforcement-like learning problem. In the T-Maze learning task the agent uses the memory bank to display adaptive behavior that normally requires a plastic ANN, thereby suggesting a complementary and effective mechanism for adaptive behavior in NE.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Greve, Rasmus Boll","Jacobsen, Emil Juul","Risi, Sebastian","Greve, Rasmus Boll"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384302"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["adaptive neural networks learning memory neural plasticity neural turing machine"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving neural turing machines for reward based learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84985896541","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384302","identifier":[{"id":"84985896541","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cf046594-fab3-4569-8ff4-992c15f237ff"],"keyword":["adaptive neural networks, learning, memory, neural plasticity, neural turing machine"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5041411495902E87595F01A679DAC137"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Boll","key":"greverasmusbollpau","last":"Greve","name":"Greve, Rasmus Boll","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil Juul","key":"jacobsenemiljuulpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Emil Juul","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risisebastianpau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908812.2908930","isbn":["9781450342063"],"pages":"117-124","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84985896541"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cf046594-fab3-4569-8ff4-992c15f237ff"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving Neural Turing Machines for Reward-based Learning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384302","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Veenstra, Frank","Faina, Andres","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382025"],"event":{"end":"2015-10-07","place":"Laubusch, de","start":"2015-10-05","title":"Workshop on \"Methods for Self-Organizing Distributed Systems\"","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evolving self organizing simulated plant inspired robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382025","ids":["itu-33b11ae2-1485-4b88-93c0-e28bed2e1f98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C23D9487116FAB941EA7A22BCEA7582D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frank","key":"veenstrapau","last":"Veenstra","name":"Veenstra, Frank","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andres","key":"fainapau","last":"Faina","locid":"7dd48cfe-3069-4563-bef4-ef661c18387a","name":"Faina, Andres","orcid":"0000-0001-7288-6988","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"støypau","last":"Støy","locid":"2a9c0934-98ca-4101-b829-b88d77f6487e","name":"Støy, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-2487","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-33b11ae2-1485-4b88-93c0-e28bed2e1f98"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evolving self-organizing simulated plant-inspired robots","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382025","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Besides the life-as-it-could-be driver of artificial life research there is also the concept of extending natural life by creating hybrids or mixed societies that are built from natural and artificial components. In this paper we motivate and present the research program of the project flora robotica. Our objective is to develop and to investigate closely linked symbiotic relationships between robots and natural plants and to explore the potentials of a plant-robot society able to produce architectural artifacts and living spaces. These robot-plant bio-hybrids create synergies that allow for new functions of plants and robots. They also create novel design opportunities for an architecture that fuses the design and construction phase. The bio-hybrid is an example of mixed societies between ‘hard artificial and ‘wet natural life, which enables an interaction between natural and artificial ecologies. They form an embodied, self-organizing, and distributed cognitive system which is supposed to grow and develop over long periods of time resulting in the creation of meaningful architectural structures. A key idea is to assign equal roles to robots and plants in order to create a highly integrated, symbiotic system. Besides the gain of knowledge, this project has the objective to create a bio-hybrid system with a defined function and application – growing architectural artifacts.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hamann, Heiko","Wahby, Mostafa","Schmickl, Thomas","Zahadat, Payam","Hofstadler, Daniel","Støy, Kasper","Risi, Sebastian","Faina, Andres","Veenstra, Frank","Kernbach, Serge","Kuksin, Igor","Kernbach, Olga","Ayers, Phil","Wojtaszek, Przemyslaw"],"cuid":["S02-089.67-012432"],"event":{"acronym":"IEEE SSCI","end":"2015-12-10","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2015-12-07","title":"2015 IEEE Symposium on Artifical Life","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Poland"],"glorg":["Adam Mickiewicz University","All Global Affiliations","Cybertronica UG (Haftungsbeschrankt)","University of Graz","University of Paderborn"],"keyword":["Architecture","Artificial Life","Bio hybrid","Bio hybrid systems","Plants","Robots","Self organizing systems","architectural artifacts","plant robot symbiosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-RDKA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"flora robotica mixed societies of symbiotic robot plant bio hybrids","src":["arkc","itu"],"src-code":["DI-ART-RDKA","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.67-012432","identifier":[{"id":"84964937762","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["arkc-8a5ce1d1-e2e0-4c7d-9e51-2001d8744f9a","itu-4181dddd-1be3-4361-8109-ca1419e73d88"],"keyword":["Architecture","Bio-hybrid","No","Plants","Robots","architectural artifacts","artificial life","bio-hybrid systems","plant-robot symbiosis","self-organizing systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB54DC9B986B7E29B1E706A371F1092E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80993764/IEEE_ALIFE_2015.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SSCI.2015.158","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of paderborn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Paderborn","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"it