{"abstract":"In DNA-templated synthesis, reactants are attached to DNA strands and complementary DNA strands are used to control the reaction towards a goal compound. This very general, simple, and still efficient approach has proven to be successful for the design of complex one-pot synthesis for a large variety of compounds. For a given goal compound many different synthesis plans may exist, and all of them can potentially be implemented with many different DNA-templated programs. This raises the issue of how to automatically infer optimal low-level programs based on a high-level synthesis plan or a goal compound only. In this paper we will introduce a computational approach for DNA-templated synthesis based on graph rewriting approaches and the systematic exploration of chemical spaces. We will use them for verification of correctness of real-world synthesis plans as well as to illustrate the non-triviality of finding an optimal DNA assembler program.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Jakob L.","Flamm, Christoph","Hanczyc, Martin M.","Merkle, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-604794"],"event":{"end":"2014-07-26","place":"New York, us","start":"2014-07-23","title":"ALife 14","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Trento","University of Vienna"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards an optimal dna templated molecular assembler","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7551/978-0-262-32621-6-ch090","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-604794","identifier":[{"id":"85064143567","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6e67b08b-8aa5-4fc8-8c7f-afd41ffaf7eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1DF1EAE085AD9B890529F6D5011A2F07"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7551/978-0-262-32621-6-ch090","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of trento","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Trento","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Lykke","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"38c5c161-3e4f-4449-8603-75cbe2967e0d","name":"Andersen, Jakob L.","name_org":"Andersen, Jakob Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-4165-3732","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"flammpau","last":"Flamm","name":"Flamm, Christoph","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin M.","key":"hanczycpau","last":"Hanczyc","name":"Hanczyc, Martin M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"merklepau","last":"Merkle","locid":"4fc26f23-4c3b-4646-a489-2df5f5635baa","name":"Merkle, Daniel","orcid":"0000-0001-7792-375X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hiroki","key":"sayamapedh","last":"Sayama","name":"Sayama, Hiroki","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolec