{"abstract":"The robustness of animal behavior is unmatched by current machines, which often falter when exposed to unforeseen conditions. While animals are notably reactive to changes in their environment, machines often follow finely tuned yet inflexible plans. Thus, instead of the traditional approach of training such machines over many different unpredictable scenarios in detailed simulations (which is the most intuitive approach to inducing robustness), this work proposes to train machines to be reactive to their environment. The idea is that robustness may result not from detailed internal models or finely tuned control policies but from cautious exploratory behavior. Supporting this hypothesis, robots trained to navigate mazes with a reactive disposition prove more robust than those trained over many trials yet not rewarded for reactive behavior in both simulated tests and when embodied in real robots. The conclusion is that robustness may neither require an accurate model nor finely calibrated behavior.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lehman, Joel","Risi, Sebastian","D'Ambrosio, David","Stanley, Kenneth O"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381720"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Space and Naval Warfare Systems Center Pacic"],"keyword":["Neural networks","Neuroevolution","Robot control","Robustness","Transfer","machine leaming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"encouraging reactivity to create robust machines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1059712313487390","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381720","identifier":[{"id":"84887485964","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1e5564aa-6f1f-4e11-95c2-6005da6d540e"],"keyword":["machine leaming","neural networks","neuroevolution","robot control","robustness","transfer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-61807028CE57C0E6367D7418B3492481"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1059712313487390","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"space and naval warfare systems center pacic","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Space and Naval Warfare Systems Center Pacic","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joel","key":"lehmanpau","last":"Lehman","name":"Lehman, Joel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"dambrosiopau","last":"D'Ambrosio","name":"D'Ambrosio, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth O","key":"stanleypau","last":"Stanley","name":"Stanley, Kenneth O","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1059712313487390","issn":["10597123","17412633"],"issn_org":["10597123"],"issue":"6","journal":"Adaptive Behavior","pages":"484-500","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Adaptive Behavior","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1e5564aa-6f1f-4e11-95c2-6005da6d540e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Encouraging reactivity to create robust machines","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381720","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Risi, Sebastian","Cellucci, Daniel","Lipson, Hod"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383298"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ribosomal robots evolved designs inspired by protein folding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463403","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383298","identifier":[{"id":"84883127585","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8aeec0dc-9b7d-44db-b90d-cba0fddd0ed0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D2150065197906FFD077432DBDE96F94"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463403","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"celluccipau","last":"Cellucci","name":"Cellucci, Daniel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hod","key":"lipsonpau","last":"Lipson","name":"Lipson, Hod","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2463372.2463403","isbn":["9781450319638"],"pages":"263-270","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GECCO '13","title":"Proceeding of the fifteenth annual conference on Genetic and evolutionary computation conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8aeec0dc-9b7d-44db-b90d-cba0fddd0ed0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ribosomal robots: Evolved designs inspired by protein folding","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383298","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Legged robots can potentially venture beyond the limits of wheeled vehicles. While creating controllers for such robots by hand is possible, evolutionary algorithms are an alternative that can reduce the burden of hand-crafting robotic controllers. Although major evolutionary approaches to legged locomotion can generate oscillations through popular techniques such as continuous time recurrent neural networks (CTRNNs) or sinusoidal input, they typically face a challenge in maintaining long-term stability. The aim of this paper is to address this challenge by introducing an effective alternative based on a new type of neuron called a single-unit pattern generator (SUPG). The SUPG, which is indirectly encoded by a compositional pattern producing network (CPPN) evolved by HyperNEAT, produces a flexible temporal activation pattern that can be reset and repeated at any time through an explicit trigger input, thereby allowing it to dynamically recalibrate over time to maintain stability. The SUPG approach, which is compared to CTRNNs and sinusoidal input, is shown to produce natural-looking gaits that exhibit superior stability over time, thereby providing a new alternative for evolving oscillatory locomotion.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Morse, Gregory","Risi, Sebastian","Snyder, Charles R","Stanley, Kenneth O"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383590"],"event":{"acronym":"GECCO","title":"Genetic and Evolutionary Computation Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Evolutionary algorithms","HyperNEAT","Legged Robotics","Locomotion Stability","Single Unit Pattern Generator SUPG"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single unit pattern generators for quadruped locomotion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463461","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383590","identifier":[{"id":"84883096501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9f790309-ecaf-4350-9b5e-8930a0096a8f"],"keyword":["Evolutionary Algorithms","HyperNEAT","Legged Robotics","Locomotion Stability","Single-Unit Pattern Generator (SUPG)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0EA7E529857F2FBB12D631073FE118DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2463372.2463461","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Robotics, Evolution, and Art Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, Culture and Games"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory","key":"morsepau","last":"Morse","name":"Morse, Gregory","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","locid":"a420ffb3-2ca6-4925-a25f-baaa5228fc15","name":"Risi, Sebastian","orcid":"0000-0003-3607-8400","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charles R","key":"snyderpau","last":"Snyder","name":"Snyder, Charles R","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth O","key":"stanleypau","last":"Stanley","name":"Stanley, Kenneth O","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2463372.2463461","isbn":["9781450319638"],"pages":"719-726","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GECCO '13","title":"Proceedings of the 15th annual conference on Genetic and evolutionary computation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9f790309-ecaf-4350-9b5e-8930a0096a8f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Single-unit pattern generators for quadruped locomotion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383590","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
